{"id":"calendar-click-mints","parent":"feat-dates","ord":"a8","title":"Clicking an empty calendar day silently creates a document #bug","done":"2026-08-21T20:43:33-04:00","desc":"- Today a day cell has two meanings behind one gesture: a day with content links to /d/&lt;date&gt;, but an EMPTY day click mints that day's note and lands in its editor (Calendar.tsx:101, Day.tsx:180). A navigation gesture writes a file — and a day cell is the smallest click target in the app, so a misclick creates a document to trash.\n- Worse, the calendar cell is the ONLY mint site: a day that already has entries links to the day view, which offers no way to create that day's note at all.\n\n**Fix (ruled):**\n- Clicking ANY day always navigates to /d/&lt;date&gt;. An empty day shows the honest empty state (\"nothing dated this day\").\n- The day page gains an explicit \"+ day note\" button, shown on any day without a note — entries or not.\n- The creation code is reused unchanged: the docDay verb (server reads the vault's daily-note convention), mintAndOpen into the editor, the undo record, the verbatim refusal. Only the trigger moves from the calendar cell to the button.\n\n**pr** — every day cell navigates, the honest empty state, minting explicit via + day note on the day page (DayMint.tsx), creation code trigger-moved unchanged","created":"2026-08-21T19:16:34-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21 (UX review of the calendar click)","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/e9640603","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/333"}}
{"id":"new-file-bare-name","parent":"feat-nav","ord":"aP","title":"+ New outline / + New document refuse a bare name: `Foo` should mint Foo.olai (and Foo.md), `Foo.olai` still accepted #next #bug","done":"2026-08-22T03:58:32-04:00","desc":"- Sidebar `+ New outline`, type `Foo`, Enter → the box shows the ops layer's refusal verbatim: \"`Foo` is not a relative `.olai` path under the served directory (no absolute path, no `..`, no `.`, and the name must end in `.olai`)\" — instead of creating `Foo.olai`. Same door, same defect for `+ New document` and `.md` (one box serves both: web/src/client/file/NewFile.tsx + making.ts; the refusal is plan.ts's create_outline / create_document validation).\n- **Ruled:** the box accepts BOTH `Foo` and `Foo.olai` (`Foo.md` for the document door) — a bare name takes the door's own suffix; a name already carrying it is taken as is; a name carrying the OTHER suffix (`Foo.md` typed into the outline door) is the one honest refusal left, said in the box's own words. Paths with folders (`notes/plan`) get the same treatment.\n- Where: the client completes the name before asking the ops layer (the door KNOWS its kind — `Making.of`), so the ops contract stays strict and one spelling; the placeholder/aria can say the suffix is optional. The refusal that remains must be the box's sentence, not the wire's paragraph.\n\n**pr** — the box completes a bare name with the door's suffix (Foo → Foo.olai / Foo.md, notes/plan → notes/plan.olai), takes Foo.olai as is, refuses the other kind's suffix in its own words, and passes `.`/`..`/trailing-separator texts through to the planner's paragraph; MCP contract untouched; 3 assumptions for the human (Foo.txt → Foo.txt.olai; Foo. completes, .. does not; the sentence's wording)","created":"2026-08-21T22:07:28-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21 ~22:05, with a screenshot: typed Foo into + New outline, got the ops layer's path refusal","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/6b464c99","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/340","ruled":"the human: the box accepts both `Foo` and `Foo.olai`, naturally — queued into the overnight campaign (lane-nob)"}}
{"id":"markdown-raw-flash","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aL","title":"Markdown flashes as RAW SOURCE for a moment before it renders — documents, notes, titles, chat, palette rows #needs-brainstorm #now #bug","done":"2026-08-24T18:52:32-04:00","desc":"**Filed** by the human 2026-08-22 ~07:40 (saw a `.md` page arrive as raw text, then become HTML a split second later); ruled then: file for NOW, fix needs brainstorming. **Fix shape 4 ruled** 2026-08-24 and dispatched (see the props for the lane facts).\n\n**The glitch.** A `.md` page (and every other markdown surface) paints its escaped SOURCE first and swaps to rendered HTML a moment later. It is written down as intended (\"raw text now, rendered a moment later\" — Markdown.tsx, chunk.ts): the remark+rehype pipeline is a lazy chunk (~95 KB brotli) fetched the first time something on the page asks, and while `markdownReady()` is false the component draws the file's own text `pre-wrap`, chosen over a blank or a spinner. Two consequences: (1) on a first visit / after a deploy the marks are visible for the fetch's duration; (2) even with the chunk cached (immutable asset) there is still at least one painted frame of source, because the first synchronous render happens before the dynamic `import()` resolves. So it is structural, not a timing accident.\n\n**Where it happens** — every caller of render.ts's guarded entry points (Markdown.tsx's `innerHTML = html() ?? escapeHtml(source)`): a tree row whose title has markdown (plain titles skip the pipeline via plain.ts), the ¶ notes (Note.tsx), the day page's note (DayNote.tsx), the document body / previews / referrers (DocumentPage.tsx + faces.tsx + DocRef.tsx), agent messages in the chat panel (Entry.tsx), palette and search hits with markdown titles (items.ts, row.ts + Result.tsx).\n\n**Fix shapes, for the brainstorm** (the human: progress feedback on loading pages is probably part of it):\n1. Route-level readiness — a page whose content is markdown-first (document, day-with-note, chat) waits for the chunk under ONE boundary before its first paint, with honest progress feedback (the page says it is loading, never shows source); outlines still paint without it; `modulepreload` the pipeline chunk from the shell so the wait is ~0 after the first visit.\n2. Fold the pipeline back into the main bundle — +95 KB brotli on first paint, cached thereafter, zero flash everywhere; simplest.\n3. Never draw source — hold the previous rendering or a height-preserving placeholder while waiting (still a blank blink on first load without feedback).\n4. **Skeleton/shimmer — the human's pointer (2026-08-24), RULED as the fix: do what modern web apps do for a loading document — the page looks loaded but the text is fuzzy.** The honest version of it here: draw the SOURCE the component already has, but illegible — blurred (CSS filter) with a soft shimmer sweep — so the layout and height are truthful (they come from the real text, not from invented gray bars), no frame of legible raw markdown is ever painted, and the swap to rendered HTML is a de-blur rather than a reflow. Works identically at every surface because it wraps the same waiting state; pairs with 1's modulepreload so the shimmer is one frame in the cached case. The skeleton IS the progress feedback — nothing extra to invent.\nWhatever the shape: one rule for all the surfaces above, and a scenario that pins \"no frame of raw markdown is ever painted\" (the `data-markdown=\"waiting\"` attribute already names the state).\n\n**merge** — the human approves personally\n\n**dispatched** — fix shape 4 ruled)","created":"2026-08-22T07:30:10-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:07-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/mrf.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T16:20:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/e3a485b9","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/369","worktree":".worktrees/markdown-raw-flash"}}
{"id":"opencode-send-silent","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"ac","title":"A turn that ends having said nothing is drawn as nothing — opencode's auth failure comes back as an empty end_turn #bug","done":"2026-08-22T11:50:44-04:00","desc":"- Reported 2026-08-22 on the deployed server (kolu-bot, user toor) right after #336: pick opencode, send a message — the row appears, then nothing. Header `opencode  Juspay/kimi-k3  0/256k`. Journal: zero chat lines.\n- **Why opencode failed there (deployment, not olai code):** its config reads the LiteLLM key as `\"apiKey\": \"{env:JUSPAY_API_KEY}\"`, and the olai systemd user unit's environment carries only PATH — the opencode olai spawns has no key. Fix: `systemd.user.services.olai.Service.EnvironmentFile` (or an HM `environmentFile` option) holding the key; docs/running.md should say an agent olai spawns inherits the SERVER's environment, not your shell's. (The `opencode run` error on that host — `no such column: replacement_seq` — is an unrelated opencode CLI-path bug.)\n- **Why olai drew nothing — REPRODUCED locally, pixel-identical to the report (screenshots in the session scratchpad):** with a broken provider key, opencode 1.17.9 does NOT return a JSON-RPC error through the ACP client: it sends `available_commands_update`, then `usage_update {used:0,size:256000}`, then answers `session/prompt` with a SUCCESSFUL `{stopReason:\"end_turn\", usage: 0 tokens}`. No message chunk, no error. (A direct driver on the host once got `-32603 No api key passed in` instead — that shape IS drawn: chat.ts:1018 publishes the notice unconditionally, traced end to end. The silent end_turn is the one that matches the screen.)\n- **The mechanism in chat.ts:** the success branch has NO arm for \"the turn succeeded and the agent said nothing\" — `outcome` is `Success(\"end_turn\")` (chat.ts:1000), settle (1016), the only check is `=== \"cancelled\"` (1051), then `move({status:\"idle\", trouble:null})` (1057). The `heard`/`quietSince` evidence (996/1030) lives only inside the Failure branch. And `\"usage\"` is in SPOKE (275-280), so a zero-token usage frame counts as \"the agent worked on it\" — which is exactly the case where it didn't.\n\n**Fix:**\n1. In the success branch, before going idle: if nothing a person can see arrived this turn (no `said`, no `tool`, no `asked` — a narrower set than SPOKE; `usage` alone is the auth-failure signature), publish a notice row (\"the agent finished without saying anything — check its provider key / `opencode auth login`\") and leave `trouble` set. Honest for every agent, free on a normal turn.\n2. Drop `usage` from the evidence that suppresses `markUndelivered` (split SPOKE: what-a-person-can-see vs has-anything-arrived for cancel), so a -32603 after a zero-token usage frame still marks the row unsent with send-again.\n3. A running turn gets a visible busy face (the composer's orange border is focus styling only).\n4. Pin with a scripted opencode-shaped agent answering `end_turn` + a lone `usage_update`.\n- Logging is chat-lifecycle-logs.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as a314683c","created":"2026-08-22T07:36:17-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:10-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22, on the deployed instance after #336","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/343"}}
{"id":"chats-list-per-agent","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"ad","title":"The chats list shows only the current agent's conversations — Claude's vanish after an opencode chat #bug","done":"2026-08-22T11:50:45-04:00","desc":"- With Claude and opencode both installed: create one opencode chat and the \"chats\" list shows only opencode sessions; every Claude conversation is gone from view until you create a NEW Claude chat just to see them.\n- **Mechanism (verified):** `chat.ts:1351` `sessions: onAgent(agent => agent.sessions)` — `onAgent` resolves `talking`, the one chosen agent; `agent.ts:941-955` `storedFor` sends `session/list` on the single running child and filters to the cwd. The roster already knows every installed agent (`agents/roster.ts:151,168`), but only the chosen row is ever spawned.\n- **Fix:** `chat.sessions` fans out over `roster()` rather than `talking`: ask each installed agent's `session/list` (spawning lazily, or a cached answer with a short TTL so opening the list doesn't start three subprocesses), tag each `SessionInfo` with its agent id (one added wire field), merge newest-first. `Sessions.tsx` groups by agent with its icon; picking a row from another agent switches the panel to that agent the way `newSession` already does. One-agent-at-a-time stays true at the process level, not at the list.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as a314683c","created":"2026-08-22T07:36:17-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:10-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22, on the deployed instance after #336","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/343"}}
{"id":"send-during-boot-doubles","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"ae","title":"A message sent while a freshly picked agent is still booting can be delivered twice #bug","done":"2026-08-22T11:50:46-04:00","desc":"- Reproduced (shots in the session scratchpad): pick an agent, type and send before the boot settles — two identical user rows and two agent answers.\n- **Mechanism:** `deliver`'s permit (chat.ts ~815) serializes deliveries against each other but not against the `opening()` permit in agent.ts:1384; a send landing in the newSession window races the open and produces two full turns. The client also reports `idle` for the first frames after `surface/chat/newSession` goes out (the panel isn't `booting` yet when the click lands).\n- **Fix:** `+ new` / the picker flips the panel to `booting` synchronously on the click, and the server's `send` takes the same permit `opening` holds, so a prompt typed during a boot queues behind exactly one open instead of racing it. Pin with a scenario that sends during the boot window.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as a314683c","created":"2026-08-22T07:56:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:10-04:00","custom":{"from":"found by the 2026-08-22 repro of opencode-send-silent","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/343"}}
{"id":"inbox-count-counts-done","parent":"feat-nav","ord":"aQ","title":"The Inbox badge counts done rows — says 3 over an inbox that draws empty #bug","done":"2026-08-22T17:10:52-04:00","desc":"- `inboxHeldOf` (format/src/inbox.ts:80) counts `rootsOf(derived, file).length` — every top-level node of the inbox, marks ignored. A processed (done) row keeps inflating the badge while the page shows nothing, so the door says 3 over an empty room.\n- **Fix (the human's ruling):** the count is what still awaits processing — top-level rows NOT marked done. A bullet or a todo/doing counts; a done row doesn't. One filter in `inboxHeldOf`, its unit test beside it, and the badge agrees with the page again.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as 6491980b","created":"2026-08-22T12:32:28-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 (screenshot: Inbox badge 3, page empty; the 3 were done)","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/348"}}
{"id":"inbox-count-headers","parent":"inbox-count-counts-done","ord":"a0","title":"The Inbox badge still says 1 over a finished branch — a bare-bullet HEADER whose children are all done is not \"awaiting processing\" #bug","done":"2026-08-22T17:10:52-04:00","desc":"#348 made `inboxHeldOf` count top-level rows whose stored mark is not `done` — and \"a bullet counts\". The Inbox's `Deferrals` root is a bare-bullet header with 10/10 done children: it counts as 1 while nothing under it awaits processing, and the page shows exactly that finished branch. The rule needs one more clause: a top-level bullet WITH children counts only if some descendant is unfinished (todo/doing, or a bullet leaf); a leaf bullet still counts; a branch whose every task is done does not. Done-marked roots stay excluded as today; mirrors/placements stay excluded. One filter in `inboxHeldOf`, unit tests beside it (finished branch → not counted; branch with one todo → counted; leaf bullet → counted), the docs that state the rule updated (docs/editing.md, docs/format.md, packages/format/README.md and the surface/web READMEs that #348 touched).\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-22 as 2de9cd19","created":"2026-08-22T16:15:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T17:10:52-04:00","custom":{"dispatch":"resume the same Grok session that shipped #348 (grok --continue in .worktrees/inbox-count-counts-done); opencode reviewer; auto-merge on verification","from":"the human 2026-08-22 16:30 (screenshot: Inbox badge 1; the page shows only `Deferrals ¶ 10/10`); ruled the same minute: a bullet with children counts only if something under it is unfinished; a leaf bullet still counts; a finished branch doesn't","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/351"}}
{"id":"runtime-dir-flood","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"aN","title":"PR: servers delete their lock file on exit and sweep dead ones on start; the e2e harness kills its servers #now #bug","done":"2026-08-23T14:30:22-04:00","desc":"Found 2026-08-23 on the human's machine: `/run/user/1000/olai/` held 163,765 files (151,369 `.lock` from the one-server-per-vault lock, #186; 12,396 `.sock` from the old `olai mcp` rendezvous socket, #175, retired the same day by #184) — 592 MB, growing since Aug 15, one per scratch vault the tests ever started. And 230 `olai web` processes from Aug 21–22 were still running on directories that no longer existed.\n\nFix (PR #355):\n1. A server removes its lock file when it stops.\n2. On start, a server sweeps the runtime directory: any `.lock` nothing holds (the kernel's flock is free) and any leftover `.sock` is deleted. A held lock is never touched — the kernel stays the one keeper of \"one brain per vault\".\n3. A spawned test server dies with its parent (Linux `PR_SET_PDEATHSIG`), and the e2e harness kills its servers before deleting their directories and on Ctrl-C/SIGTERM (then exits 130/143). (A server whose vault is deleted under it shows the \"unreadable directory\" banner and stays up — that is the store's ratified contract, so \"exit when the root disappears\" was dropped.)\n4. Every test process gets its own runtime directory, set once by the bun test preload, so `just test` can never touch the developer's real one.\nEvidence in the PR: before 163,765 → 14 on this machine; the isolation probe (zero names from the suite in the real dir, re-run by the reviewer); unit red→green; the cancelled-run pin.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-23 as 4d6056db, approved by the human","created":"2026-08-23T12:12:23-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:09-04:00","custom":{"follow-up-observed":"2026-08-23 16:25 — the #354 lane's demo recording hit #355's getppid()===1 self-SIGTERM in practice (a server whose spawner exits reparents to PID 1 and kills itself mid-recording); opencode's nit on #355 said exactly this (\"any daemonising wrapper would self-SIGTERM\"). Workaround: keep the server a child of the recorder. If it bites again, the check should gate on the spawn shape rather than getppid — a small follow-up, not filed yet.","from":"orchestrator RCA 2026-08-23 while chasing the wrong-vault capture; the human: its own lane, Grok now, opencode reviewer","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/355","ruled":"the human 2026-08-23 12:30: its own lane, spawned by Grok right now, opencode reviewer; the PR waits for the human's approval","where":"packages/server/src/lock.ts (the `<digest>.lock` in runtimeHome()), serve.ts:398 (not unlinked on teardown), the e2e harness's serve spawning (packages/tests)"}}
{"id":"agenda-only-todo","parent":"feat-dates","ord":"a9","title":"PR: the agenda lists only todo items #now #bug","done":"2026-08-23T15:42:59-04:00","desc":"Today the agenda shows every dated node that is not done — including bare bullets with a date (occurrences: a birthday, a note pinned to a day). The human wants the agenda to show only work: dated nodes marked `todo` (and `doing`, a started todo). Occurrences stay on their day page and in the calendar dots, off the agenda.\n\nWhere: `packages/format/src/agenda.ts` — `unfinished` is `storedMarker(node) !== \"done\"`; it should be the format's own `Unfinished` (todo | doing). The overdue count / the burning Agenda entry follow the same predicate. Docs that describe the agenda (docs/format.md \"Due dates\", docs/editing.md, brainstorming/agenda.md if it states the rule) say the new rule. Tests pin: a dated bullet is not on the agenda; a dated todo is; a dated doing is; done never.\n\n**pr** — merged 2026-08-23 as 5bc09d66, approved by the human","created":"2026-08-23T14:21:00-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-23 14:25: 'agenda should only contain todo items'","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/356","ruled":"Grok author, opencode reviewer; the human approves the PR"}}
{"id":"compact-lost-to-steer","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"af","title":"Sends queue by default, steering becomes the explicit gesture — the /compact abort is one symptom #bug","done":"2026-08-24T15:25:34-04:00","desc":"- **The human's reframe (2026-08-24): this bug is not about compaction.** It is about the panel supporting QUEUING (and optionally steering). With queuing as the default, the compaction abort gets sorted out implicitly — a queued message waits behind whatever is running and pre-empts nothing.\n- **The symptom that surfaced it (screenshot):** `/compact` → \"Compacting...\" → a message sent while it ran steered — and the compaction died: *\"Compacting failed: API Error: Request was aborted. Compaction canceled.\"* The turn proceeded on the uncompacted context. Steering pre-empts by design (`_session/steering` at the SDK's `now` priority, `packages/chat/src/agents/claude.ts:283`); compaction is a request whose abort destroys the work.\n- **History:** the panel HAD a queue; `chat-steer-on-send` (#194) deleted it and made every send steer. What #194 rightly killed was the client-side queue's sins — words held invisibly out of the session, destroyed by cancel's `dropQueue`. It over-corrected by making pre-emption the only delivery.\n- **Upstream, confirmed 2026-08-24:** core ACP's schema has NO `promptQueueing` — the spec neither defines nor forbids a mid-turn `session/prompt`. The pinned adapter (`agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp`) queues it for real and SAYS so: a `turnQueue` FIFO — \"later entries are queued and will be echoed in order\" (`src/acp-agent.ts:447`) — advertised at initialize as `agentCapabilities._meta.claudeCode.promptQueueing: true`; steering advertised beside it (`_meta.steering.supported`). So the queue olai needs is the adapter's own, no upstream ask for the core behavior; the capability bit is what a leg reads to know it is there.\n- **Ruled (the human, 2026-08-24, question tool):**\n  - **Send = plain `session/prompt`, always** — busy or idle, one verb, one code path. Idle simply starts the turn; busy is held by the adapter's FIFO and delivered when the running work (turn, compaction, whatever) ends. No client-side queue state, no compaction awareness anywhere.\n  - **Steering stays, as a modifier on send** (Alt+Enter-shaped; a deliberate variant on phone) — plain Enter queues, the modifier steers into the running turn. Interruption is always on purpose.\n  - **Cancel stops the turn and nothing else** — queued messages survive at the adapter and run next, in order. #194's \"cancel means stop-the-agent and nothing else\" stands; words are never touched.\n- **UX:** send anytime; the row lands in the transcript at once, wearing a \"queued\" hint while the agent is busy; the hint clears when the agent takes it. The modifier send is the one interrupting gesture. The `/compact` abort becomes impossible without the panel ever learning what compaction is.\n- Note: opencode's leg already lives in this world (no steering method, -32601; every send is a prompt) — the claude leg converging on prompt-by-default makes the two legs one story, with steering as the claude leg's extra gesture where advertised.\n\n**pr** — 2026-08-24 15:28 — sends queue by default (plain session/prompt always, the adapter's FIFO), steering the explicit modifier where advertised, cancel touches nothing queued, the queued hint truthful across reload; the /compact abort impossible; PLUS the human-arbitrated guard: interrupt withdraws once the session has queued (until claude-agent-acp#1039 is fixed upstream); two evidence-run defects and both reviews' findings folded; grok OBJECT resolved by the human's ruling, pi's counterargument recorded in the PR","see":["chat-steer-on-send"],"created":"2026-08-24T11:10:16-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:10-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-24 — /compact + mid-compaction send in the ACP chat panel; screenshot of the abort","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/0264ca47","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/366"}}
{"id":"mrf-implement","parent":"markdown-raw-flash","ord":"a0","title":"Build the blurred-placeholder fix, open the PR, record the evidence #bug","done":"2026-08-24T18:22:51-04:00","desc":"Reported at 17:00 (terminal 8ad34c07), then REBASED at 18:20 on the orchestrator's order to strip commits: the two commits that would have broken master were DROPPED (their widening of `wordIn` was the shape arbitration had rejected; PR #371's narrowing version rules instead). The base is now origin/master through PR #372, so PRs #367, #368 and #372 sit underneath it, and packages/chat is untouched.\n\nThe evidence was NOT re-recorded: the client source tree was diffed and is byte-identical between the two tips, and the evidence section was re-run against master's chat helpers (nine screenshots, no errors). Local checks at the rebased head: typecheck 15 of 15, 3613 unit tests passing with none failing, plus 77 browser tests. CI at commit bf50eb1: 9 of 10 green, with the end-to-end job still running under a fail-fast wait.\n\nWhat the PR does (fix the blurred placeholder): `renderTitle` now answers with which stage it is at (`TitleDrawing.waiting`); plain titles, about 95% of them, never show the placeholder at all; the third state belongs to the arrival — a page whose renderer never loads keeps its source legible, a defect the author found in its own first attempt and covered with a scenario. The app shell preloads the markdown pipeline chunk right after the stylesheet at low fetch priority (+93 KB brotli on first paint; the reversal of the earlier ruling is recorded). A test pins that removing the blur does not move the block.\n\n**Incident owned:** this lane's `pkill -f cucumber` killed the coordinator of another running lane, which had to re-run.\n\n**Worth filing separately:** Referrers.tsx never renders markdown at all, so markdown marks show permanently there — out of scope here.\n\n**PR:** at commit bf50eb1.","created":"2026-08-24T16:09:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:01:52-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/369","terminal":"8ad34c07"}}
{"id":"mrf-review-grok","parent":"markdown-raw-flash","ord":"a1","title":"Review of the markdown-flash fix, by the grok agent #bug","done":"2026-08-24T18:32:29-04:00","desc":"The grok agent reviewed the PR and did not object, with zero must-fix findings (finished 18:31 after 8 minutes 26 seconds, reviewing by reading the code only — it ran no test suites). Comment: https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/369#issuecomment-5402357805\n\nVerified by reading: that the rebase really left the chat package untouched; that the preload of the markdown chunk sits after the stylesheet at low fetch priority, matching what the PR documents; and that the evidence really is unchanged (the production client tree is identical between the backup tip from before the rebase and the current head).\n\n- **Should fix:** arriving.test.ts line 71 never actually asserts `waiting()` — which is exactly the regression this branch had already shipped once, in one commit.\n- **Nit:** Markdown.tsx line 69 still works out the waiting state from `!ready`; what saves it is the separate `<Show>` for the failure case.","after":["mrf-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:09:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:01:52-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"fba60285"}}
{"id":"mrf-review-pi","parent":"markdown-raw-flash","ord":"a2","title":"Review of the markdown-flash fix, by the pi agent #bug","done":"2026-08-24T18:38:33-04:00","desc":"The pi agent reviewed the PR and did not object: zero must-fix findings, one should-fix, one nit (finished 18:37, reviewing by reading the code after the orchestrator aborted its test run and handed it the new reviewer contract mid-review). Comment: https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/369#issuecomment-5402426318\n\nAll five review dimensions verified by reading:\n- The two states are honestly distinguished (title.ts lines 196-199 via `markdownWaiting`, Markdown.tsx lines 74-101 via `data-markdown=failed`); no input was found that produces the wrong state, and the spelling that was historically wrong now has a regression scenario.\n- The rebase is clean: the chat package is untouched, there is no leftover of the `wordIn` or `chatSend` changes, and the base carries PRs #367, #368, #370 and #372.\n- The preload of the markdown chunk was verified in the built output — after the stylesheet, at low fetch priority — and the build fails closed if that chunk stops being split out.\n- The claim that the evidence is unchanged was verified against the tip from before the force-push.\n\n- **Should fix (substantive, flagged for the human):** faces.tsx line 145 only builds the table of contents once the markdown pipeline is ready, so on a document with two or more headings the contents block appears in the same paint as the un-blurring — a reflow at the very instant of the swap, against the ruling that the swap should be an un-blur rather than a reflow.\n- **Nit:** README.md line 102's byte figures drifted after the rebase, by 28 bytes and 194 bytes.","after":["mrf-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:09:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:01:52-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-pi","terminal":"d1c741fc"}}
{"id":"mrf-close","parent":"markdown-raw-flash","ord":"a3","title":"Fix the review findings, run CI once, hand the PR to the human #bug","done":"2026-08-24T18:52:32-04:00","desc":"Closed at 18:52 on the human's word (\"369 approved\"). The fixes were pushed at 18:48:\n- grok's should-fix is done: arriving.test.ts now asserts `waiting()` as meaning \"here, but not rendered yet\"; a failure is not waiting; and reading starts the fetch.\n- grok's nit is done: Markdown.tsx now reads `markdownWaiting()`, the same answer title.ts reads.\n- pi's nit is done: the byte figures were re-measured (+381,497 bytes raw, +92,784 bytes brotli); pi's reported drift of 28 and 194 bytes was exact.\n- pi's should-fix was defended by measurement and labelled for the human in the PR body: the table-of-contents reflow at the moment of the swap is identical on master's build (181px to 316px, contents 99px, on both sides) — the branch only changes the frame before it. The options and their costs are recorded at that point in document/faces.tsx.\n\nCI all green at 3df99309. MERGED as squash commit e3a485b9 on the human's personal approval; the worktree was removed, the branch deleted and terminal 8ad34c07 retired.","after":["mrf-review-grok","mrf-review-pi"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:09:15-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:01:52-04:00"}
{"id":"master-red-meta-merge","ord":"b01","title":"Master does not typecheck: two PRs that were each fine alone broke when merged together #now #bug","done":"2026-08-24T17:23:08-04:00","desc":"Found by one lane's author (pi) at 16:53, and independently corroborated by another lane's author, who at 16:20 had reported it as \"pre-existing on master\". Two defects, both born from this afternoon's merges being individually green and wrong together:\n\n1. **The typecheck break.** PR #336 (2026-08-22) widened the `Meta` type in leg.ts to `record | null | undefined`. PR #365 then landed `stringIn`, which passes `claudeIn(meta)` — a full `Meta` — into `wordIn`, which accepts only `record | undefined`. `tsc --noEmit` therefore fails in @olai/chat and @olai/server. The one-word repair: `wordIn` should take `Meta` (claude.ts line 346).\n2. **The end-to-end test helper collision.** PR #365 and PR #366 each added their own block of constants and helpers to their feature sections, both defining CHAT_TOGGLE, PANEL, INPUT, SEND, TRANSCRIPT and `openChat`. They need to become one shared block, keeping #366's `openChat`, which waits for the agent — #365's section needs that wait anyway.\n\nThe lesson for the board: two merges into adjacent chat code on the same afternoon want a cross-check CI run at the MERGED head, not only at each PR's own head.\n\n**PR:** opened 2026-08-24 17:22.\n\n**Merge:** approved by the human at 17:18 — on pi's clean verdict plus green CI, the orchestrator squash-merges without asking again.","created":"2026-08-24T16:55:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:01:52-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/mrm.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T16:58:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/69ecc2a4","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/371","worktree":".worktrees/master-red-meta-merge"}}
{"id":"mrm-implement","parent":"master-red-meta-merge","ord":"a0","title":"Make only the two repairs and open the PR #bug","done":"2026-08-24T17:08:41-04:00","desc":"Reported at 17:11 (terminal 2be35862). The decision went the other way from the node's suggestion: rather than widening `wordIn`, the fix narrows the types. `fieldIn`'s `Meta` annotation was the untruth — its `value === null` guard already consumes the wire's `_meta: null`, so both of its exits return `object | undefined`, exactly as its own doc comment said. `claudeIn` and `metaOf` inherited that untruth; the runtime behaviour was always correct. Widening `wordIn` would have advertised a case the file never produces.\n\nRepair 2: evidence.ts had not parsed since PR #366 (twelve TypeScript TS2451 duplicate-declaration errors), which also aborted a full `bun test` run through the manifest tree scan. It is now one block of selectors, keeping the richer `openChat` under the name `openChatForAgent`.\n\nSuites: typecheck 14 clean; unit tests 3593 plus 77 browser tests, none failing; end-to-end 9 of 9, covering both PRs' sections.\n\nSpotted: PR #368 carried the opposite fix privately — an order to strip it went out at 17:12.\n\n**PR:** at commit d2b59246.","created":"2026-08-24T16:55:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:01:52-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/371"}}
