{"id":"bug-validation","ord":"b04","title":"Validation & the last-good trap","done":"2026-09-03T12:17:26-04:00","desc":"The family: the set validates as a whole, so one bad write or one broken file degrades far more than itself — and the recovery doors are narrower than the failure. Grouped 2026-08-29 on the human's word, seeded by the declare-gate incident (vault commit 3f7478ad) plus the four standing bugs moved in.","created":"2026-08-29T20:38:30-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:55:58-04:00"}
{"id":"bug-declare-unfit","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"a0","title":"Declaring a type over values that don't fit is accepted — and takes the vault into last-good mode #bug","done":"2026-08-29T22:21:44-04:00","desc":"Proven live: declaring `brainstorm` type `doc` while eight existing values didn't fit was accepted, and every outline instantly showed the last good version. The write-time validator checks less than the load-time one, so a write can land that the next load refuses. Fix: declaring REFUSES while any governed value doesn't fit, naming the offenders — the same fence set_prop already gives new writes.","created":"2026-08-29T20:38:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T22:21:44-04:00","custom":{"from":"the declare-gate incident, 2026-08-29 20:27 (vault commit 3f7478ad); the Inbox entry filed here on the human's word","node":"brainstorm-declares"}}
{"id":"bug-lastgood-locked","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"a1","title":"Last-good mode locks out its own recovery — the ops layer can't see or undo the write that broke the set #bug","done":"2026-08-29T23:21:11-04:00","desc":"Once the set rolls back to last-good, the breaking write exists only on disk — the ops layer serves the older set, so the node to trash \"is not a node in the loaded set\". The one honest recovery is hand/git editing, which everything else forbids. The fix rides bug-declare-unfit (prevention) but deserves its own thought: a repair door that can address what is on DISK when disk and set disagree.","created":"2026-08-29T20:38:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T23:21:11-04:00","custom":{"from":"the same incident: trash_node on the breaking declaration refused as not-in-set — the loaded set predates the write that must be undone; git checkout on the human's order was the only door"}}
{"id":"bug-multi-error-fix","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"a2","title":"A multi-error file can't be fixed one write at a time — every corrective write is refused while the others stand #bug","done":"2026-08-29T22:21:44-04:00","desc":"Whole-file validation refuses any write that leaves the file invalid — including the write that fixes ONE of several errors. Repair therefore requires fixing everything in one atomic write (`apply` may do it; unverified) or going around the ops layer. And a bad value on a TRASHED node may have no ops-path fix at all.","created":"2026-08-29T20:38:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T22:21:44-04:00","custom":{"from":"the same incident: each corrective set_prop refused because the file still held the other bad values; untested whether a batched apply threads it, and values on trashed nodes may be unfixable by ops entirely"}}
{"id":"per-file-validation","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"a7","title":"PR: brokenness becomes per-file — one broken outline degrades alone #bug","done":"2026-08-29T23:22:24-04:00","started":"2026-08-29T20:50:32-04:00","desc":"The human's rulings 2026-08-29 20:40 (question tool): per-file everywhere (boot + runtime); a broken file's page shows ERRORS ONLY; healthy files serve and accept writes; the vault-wide banner becomes a summary naming broken files. Closes cold-boot-all-or-nothing, broken-file-blocks-healthy-writes, last-good-banner-flood, and the trap-root of bug-lastgood-locked. Night mandate: auto-merge on evidence.","created":"2026-08-29T20:49:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T23:22:24-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/per-file-validation.md","dispatched":"2026-08-29T20:52:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/441","terminal":"1142fad2","tier":"design-heavy","worktree":".worktrees/per-file-validation"}}
