{"id":"bug-ref-variant-cross-break","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"aA","title":"A write can still break a file it did not write — a ref variant moved out of its root (contained per-file, not refused) #bug","done":"2026-08-30T11:08:52-04:00","desc":"The one place #441 knowingly ships less than post-#439 master promised: moving a ref variant out of its root can invalidate the file that declared it. #439 refused that write at the store; per-file validation publishes the candidate instead, so the declaring file becomes broken and degrades alone — VISIBLE, but the write that broke it landed. Two candidate fixes are named at the pin; ruled overnight to ship pinned rather than invent an unreviewed seam in a merge commit.","created":"2026-08-29T23:03:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-30T11:08:52-04:00","custom":{"from":"#441's author, 2026-08-29 23:01 — pinned in ops.test.ts as behaviour, explicitly not endorsed, two candidate fixes named in the pin","node":"per-file-validation","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/441"}}
{"id":"752u4ddh","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"aB","title":"The no-refusal arm: a drifted file that still validates is clobbered silently, and drift in untouched files never heals #bug","done":"2026-08-30T11:27:21-04:00","desc":"#440's accepted boundary (its author's own deferral): the heal door only opens on a REFUSAL, so a write whose own file was replaced behind the store's back but whose set still validates LANDS and clobbers the replacement — and drift sitting in files the write does not touch lands as a success over a stale set. Same bug family as stale-set-reads-clean-writes-refuse (the drift check would catch both) but no refusal ever shows, so the ruled trigger never fires. Adjacent and by construction out of reach: findings whose cause is a file the verdict cannot name (unknown-target is about an id). The resync door remains the hand-heal.","created":"2026-08-30T00:31:45-04:00","changed":"2026-08-30T11:27:21-04:00","custom":{"node":"stale-set-heal","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/440"}}
{"id":"ngdh6rwn","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"aC","title":"A foreign-parent error darkens the file that was merely pointed at — the innocent parent file goes errors-only and refuses writes #bug","done":"2026-08-30T11:08:52-04:00","desc":"From #441's accepted deferral (grok graded it SHOULD). The blame axis (implicatedBy) counts every file a finding names — right for a duplicate id and a cycle, where both ends share the fault, wrong for foreign-parent: the file that DECLARES the parent did nothing but be pointed at, yet it degrades to errors-only and refuses writes. That is broken-file-blocks-healthy-writes re-entering through one error code. Two candidate fixes at different layers: a per-code fact in errors.ts's catalogue (where classifications live), or the fact on the Related value itself — note #440's merge added Related.broken:false for judge sites, which may be exactly this shape.","created":"2026-08-30T09:09:06-04:00","changed":"2026-08-30T11:08:52-04:00","custom":{"from":"#441's Deferrals, accepted overnight 2026-08-29; the human ordered the fix dispatched 2026-08-30","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/441"}}
{"id":"blame-at-fault","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"aD","title":"PR: blame lands only on the file at fault — the ref-variant move refused, the pointed-at file stays lit #bug","done":"2026-08-30T11:08:52-04:00","started":"2026-08-30T09:10:59-04:00","worked":7073,"desc":"The human's dispatch word 2026-08-30 morning (\"dispatch both today\" + the over-darkening fix). Closes bug-ref-variant-cross-break (the pinned-not-endorsed hole: a moved ref variant lands and darkens the declaring file — flip the pin to a refusal, two candidate fixes named in the pin) and the foreign-parent bug filed this morning (the pointed-at file goes errors-only for merely being pointed at — a per-code fact in errors.ts's catalogue, or the fact on the Related value, #440's Related.broken face being the possible shape). Must not weaken #441's per-file publishing, #440's pinned drift asks, or #439's declaration fence.","see":["bug-ref-variant-cross-break","ngdh6rwn"],"created":"2026-08-30T09:10:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-30T11:08:52-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/blame-at-fault.md","dispatched":"2026-08-30T09:12:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/443","terminal":"eb8820cb","tier":"design-heavy","worktree":".worktrees/blame-at-fault"}}
