{"id":"no-refusal-drift","parent":"bug-validation","ord":"aE","title":"PR: drift is caught without a refusal — a still-valid stale write stops clobbering silently #bug","done":"2026-08-30T11:27:21-04:00","started":"2026-08-30T09:11:11-04:00","worked":8170,"desc":"The human's dispatch word 2026-08-30 morning. Closes the no-refusal-arm bug (#440's accepted boundary, filed 752u4ddh): the heal only opens on a refusal, so a write whose file was replaced but still validates clobbers the replacement silently, and drift in untouched files never heals. Design to settle: where the happy path pays the check (the write's own paths at the gate is the obvious candidate) and what untouched-file drift triggers — without burning the read-vintage red line or #440's one-repair semantics. Sibling lane blame-at-fault shares the ops/format seams; second lander resolves.","see":["752u4ddh"],"created":"2026-08-30T09:11:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-30T11:27:21-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/no-refusal-drift.md","dispatched":"2026-08-30T09:12:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/442","terminal":"9cf5d7a7","tier":"design-heavy","worktree":".worktrees/no-refusal-drift"}}
