{"id":"self-sigterm-guard","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"aQ","title":"PR: a server stops killing itself when orphaned #bug","done":"2026-09-01T10:50:16-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T08:21:50-04:00","worked":8906,"desc":"A spawned server dies with its parent — that is the Linux PR_SET_PDEATHSIG guard #355 added, and it is right for the test harness. But the check it pairs with reads `getppid() === 1`, which means: if my parent is PID 1, I have been orphaned, so I should stop. That is true for a test server whose runner died. It is FALSE for every daemonising wrapper, because a wrapper's whole job is to exit and leave the child running — the child then sees PID 1 as its parent and kills itself while perfectly healthy.\n\nThis is not hypothetical: it bit once, live, on 2026-08-23 — a demo recording lost its server mid-capture, and the workaround was the awkward one (keep the server a child of the recorder). opencode's review of #355 predicted it in a nit at the time.\n\nThe fix the note names: gate on the SPAWN SHAPE rather than on getppid — a server that was told it is a child of a test runner behaves that way; one started any other way does not. Small and mechanical; the bar is a test that fails on today's check and passes on the new one, plus one that proves a wrapper-started server survives its wrapper exiting.\n\n**QUEUED (the human, 2026-08-31 ~20:45), second of the night's four lanes**, dispatched when the lane before it merges. Auto-merge.","see":["runtime-dir-flood"],"created":"2026-08-31T16:45:43-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:10-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/self-sigterm-guard.md","dispatched":"2026-09-01T08:16:00-04:00","from":"the follow-up named in runtime-dir-flood's own note (2026-08-23), surfaced as a dispatch candidate 2026-08-31","kolu-terminal":"80d5e04c","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/77264bc2","merged":"2026-09-01","odu-worktree":".worktrees/self-sigterm-guard","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/455","tier":"design-heavy","timings":"implement 26m02s (opus) · refactor 33m53s · reviews 2 rounds each 19m06s/40m45s parallel (grok/pi, 0 MUST 4 SHOULD 4 NIT) · address 2 rounds 24m45s · merge-master 5m08s (RAN — #454 landed under it) · ci 16m41s (11/11 first attempt) · close <1m — TOTAL 2h34m (08:16→10:50)"}}
