{"id":"lane-ssg-review-a","parent":"self-sigterm-guard","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #bug","done":"2026-09-01T10:15:11-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T10:08:20-04:00","worked":1146,"desc":"Approve. It spent its probe re-running the author's own three-process experiment and CONFIRMED the subreaper finding independently: with no `PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER` the orphan lands on 1 and both rules agree; with a grandparent subreaper the orphan lands on the grandparent and `orphaned_by_pid1_rule=false` while the told-pid rule still fires. It also checked the measurement METHODS rather than the results, and confirmed the red legs are red for the mechanism rather than the fixture — the kid's own log quotes #355's check firing, not a timeout.\n\nIts two SHOULDs are the kind a second pair of eyes exists for. The first: the suite never sets `PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER`, so the very claim that justifies a pid-tie OVER gating the old check is unpinned — a lesser fix would also go 6/0 on this box and still miss the race under a user session. The second is carefully not overclaimed: the test's kid exits in its own SIGTERM handler, so the race pin goes green on delivery, while in the product the SELF arm is installed later — it does not claim the product race is open, it claims the suite does not show it closed.","after":["lane-ssg-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T10:15:11-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"ec177cc8","musts":"0","reviewer":"agent-grok","shoulds":"3"}}
{"id":"lane-ssg-merge-master","parent":"self-sigterm-guard","ord":"a3","title":"merge latest master into the PR #bug","done":"2026-09-01T10:32:57-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T10:27:49-04:00","worked":308,"desc":"RAN, unlike the other three lanes today. #454 merged as 399501f4 while this lane was working, leaving the branch a commit behind, so the step did what it exists for: the CI run now tests the code as it will actually LAND rather than as it was written. Merged as a merge commit, never a rebase. No conflict — #454 was ops and format, this diff is the server's sigterm path — and the light suites were re-run at the merged head: typecheck 22/22, the touched file 8 pass / 0 fail.","after":["lane-ssg-review-a","lane-ssg-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T10:32:57-04:00"}
