{"id":"lane-ssg-evidence","parent":"self-sigterm-guard","ord":"a6","title":"evidence verified #bug","done":"2026-09-01T10:49:39-04:00","desc":"VERIFIED as proof rather than a photograph — a process-lifetime fix has no visual face, and its bar was always a test that fails on the old check and passes on the new one.\n\nWhat stands: with #355's check restored verbatim the file runs 6 pass / 2 fail; on this branch 8 / 0, three consecutive runs. Against the LESSER fix — gate the arm, keep `getppid() === 1` — it runs 6 / 2, and both failures are attributable rather than incidental: one leg arranges a kernel where `getppid()` never reads 1, the other stages the state the race leaves behind in the product, where the old rule has nothing to see.\n\nBoth reviewers independently attacked that pin. grok probed the lesser fix and showed the leg times out on it and cannot go green on it either, the two conditions being mutually exclusive. pi traced the same path and found the half that separates a real pin from a hollow one: the leg refuses its own fake-greens, since an unarmed subreaper throws at the `prctl=0` gate before it could pass on an ordinary machine, and a reparent-to-init would fail the `orphanedAt !== 1` assertion.\n\nAnd the CI watcher checked the hazard peculiar to this lane — the harness itself spawns servers — finding no unexpected deaths and no startup oddity at the merged head.","after":["lane-ssg-ci"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T10:49:39-04:00"}
