{"id":"lane-wso-review-a","parent":"wake-scope-outlines","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #bug","done":"2026-09-01T11:36:43-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T11:33:50-04:00","worked":1060,"desc":"Two rounds. Round 1 at 95977e1e: approve, no MUST, 1 SHOULD — the fix closed the door and left the key in it, since `wake.kinds` was typed against `FileKind`, which INCLUDES `document`, so a plugin could declare it, type-check green, and reproduce the screenshot defect with the heartbeat reporting a live watch over an empty set.\n\nRound 2 at 93681120: **MUST-fix.** The bound itself landed — `NodeKind` is the `holds extends \"nodes\"` complement of `BodyKind`, `KINDS` is annotated with it, and the headers, both READMEs and the body stopped offering `FileKind` as the catch. But the new PIN was hollow: the `@ts-expect-error` bindings restated `NodeKind` instead of reading `typeof wake.kinds`, so widening the wake.ts annotation back to `FileKind` left `\"document\"` spellable with all three tests green. Plus a NIT: server.ts:239 prose still said kolu types against FileKind.\n\nRound 3 at 54d0e346 (the address round finished by the grok author seat after Claude's weekly limit): **MUST landed, NIT landed, nothing remaining.** The pin reads the production slot — `type Declared = typeof wake.kinds`, every `@ts-expect-error` annotated with that; widening `KINDS` to `FileKind` with the value left `[\"outline\"]` sends the five bodied directives unused (\"hologram\" still errors, which is why the five bodied kinds, not the nonsense word, are the pin — a type still admitting any bodied kind fails typecheck). server.ts no longer claims the FileKind bound. Posted 2026-09-01 15:35Z: https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/457#issuecomment-5496418963","after":["lane-wso-refactor"],"created":"2026-09-01T09:46:44-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T11:36:43-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"927d0f69","musts":"1","reviewer":"agent-grok","shoulds":"1"}}
