{"id":"doorbell-missing-claim","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"ai","title":"PR: the doorbell misses a claimed lane #bug","done":"2026-09-01T19:41:15-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T18:11:53-04:00","worked":5362,"desc":"A lane fully claimed on the board is INVISIBLE to the fleet doorbell: no initial wake, no nag, absent from the \"whole standing set\" wake lists, uncounted by the heartbeat.\n\n**INTERIM MITIGATION (the human, 2026-09-01 ~18:25): a backstop `kolu watch` Monitor runs in the orchestrator conversation until this lane lands** — `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --heartbeat 30m --json`, persistent (task bwapgsosh). It is the retired-at-#450 Monitor, re-armed as belt-and-suspenders because the doorbell provably drops a lane; it sees the terminals the doorbell misses. HAZARD carried while it runs: the await-monitor-hang finding — a conversation that has armed a Monitor makes the interrupt button hang (queued sends are unaffected). Disarm (TaskStop) the moment this lane deploys.\n\n**ROOT CAUSE, proven (the human pushed for it, 2026-09-01 ~18:05):** the affected lane's terminal is ABSENT FROM THE WATCHER'S RINGING SET, not merely delayed. Threefold proof, each ruling out an alternative:\n- **Not nag-disabled.** `_olai/Kolu.olai` watch reads `nag: 10m` — ON. Yet task-notification-spill's terminal 11e565c0 idled with a doing step from 21:42:52Z and drew ZERO nags across 26+ minutes. An in-set idle-owed terminal nags every 10m; zero nags ⇒ not in set.\n- **Not queue starvation.** The doorbell delivered 5 wakes naming 2d3dc63c and 7 naming 4b5a3fb6 through the same continuously-busy conversation. Delivery works under load; this lane never fired.\n- **Per-terminal delivery census (transcript, kolu-watcher bodies):** 4b5a3fb6:7, 2d3dc63c:5, 5a6f3f71:4, e31ecb6f:3, 3fd756ef:3, eb275737/52023475:2, 6a75839f:1 — and **11e565c0:0, 533e1ed8:0**. Both of task-notification-spill's terminals got zero. It is the LANE, not the seat. (3ce0b574 also 0 but a red herring — never went idle-owed.)\n\n**Ruled out as mechanism:** creation method (cwd and fresh-worktree terminals both appear among the RINGING), serve restart (PID 2373093 continuous since 12:30 EDT), mirror resolution (day-mirror-tns resolves cleanly, kolu-terminal=11e565c0, doing step present).\n\n**Surviving hypothesis for the fix:** task-notification-spill's NODE PRE-EXISTED its dispatch — minted when the bug was filed, then the dispatch grafted its steps + claim + mirror onto the already-existing node; every RINGING lane's node was minted FRESH in its dispatch. The watcher's set-derivation likely fails to (re-)include a node whose CLAIM or DOING STEP was added AFTER the node first entered the board index. Pin with a regression test that reproduces RED first (the reproduce-red-first law): mint a node, THEN add its kolu-terminal + a doing child, assert the derived set includes it. Fix so the set is a true function of the CURRENT board every derivation. Ship the watcher logging in the same PR (the bug was undiagnosable because the watcher logs nothing). P1 supervision-integrity.","created":"2026-09-01T17:20:18-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:11-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/doorbell-missing-claim.md","dispatched":"2026-09-01T18:12:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-09-01 ~17:20 (\"How did you miss the Kolu event?\" / \"Does it not nag you?\") — evidenced from the watcher's own wake texts in the orchestrator conversation","kolu-terminal":"1d0d1d2c","merge":"merge-auto","odu-worktree":".worktrees/doorbell-missing-claim","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/462","tier":"design-heavy","timings":"implement 26m (test seen RED first — the law's first application) · refactor 18m · review 7m (grok, approve + the sibling hole) · address 15m · merge-master 7m · ci 5m 11/11 no flakes · dispatch→merge 1h29m"}}
