{"id":"lane-dmc-refactor","parent":"doorbell-missing-claim","ord":"a1","title":"refactor passes #bug","done":"2026-09-01T19:01:07-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T18:41:18-04:00","worked":1189,"after":["lane-dmc-implement"],"created":"2026-09-01T18:11:53-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T19:01:07-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-dmc-review-a","parent":"doorbell-missing-claim","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #bug","done":"2026-09-01T19:09:29-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T19:01:07-04:00","worked":502,"desc":"grok at 396da8a8: **APPROVE** — 0 MUST, 2 SHOULD, 2 NIT. Verified the derived ringing set is now a TRUE FUNCTION of the current Derived on every walk (claimedIn keeps no index; reached is call-local; the published snapshot is replaced whole per revision; the only memo is minted in ring and dropped with the event) — so a claim grafted later, a mirror added later, a step marked doing after the fact, or a node un-trashed each land as a new revision the next event re-walks. It also READ origin/master to settle that the test would have gone red on the old gate: `unfinished(undefined)` is false, so the mirror of an UNMARKED tns was skipped before descending — the lane dropped at the outer gate and would have dropped at the inner one too; the red isolates to the missing claim.\n\nSHOULD doorbell.ts:540 — **the next hole of the same shape**: `live = own !== undefined` still treats an unmarked node with no children as not-work even when it carries kolu-terminal, so a lane filed as a bullet and then given ONLY a terminal (claim written before the steps land) is still invisible — the P1's sibling one level down. Either say so in the header in as many words, or add the mint-then-graft-without-children case beside the P1 test so a future widening cannot call itself a regression of this one. (Also: `settled` ends the branch without adding to `reached`, so descendants that are not records of the filter file are unreachable — intentional for a verdict, but worth a sentence since set_cancelled is not branch-gated and a merge can put unfinished work under done.)\n\nSHOULD server.ts:413 — the diagnostic names the INCLUDED set (`ringing`, `unmatched`) but `fleet` is a bare count and `classified meaning=none` names the event's terminal without saying WHY it is out (not-in-file / unmatched / unmarked-leaf / settled-ancestor / not-live). The incident stays diagnosable because the watcher emits for the whole fleet, but the exclusion reason is the readable fact. Comment 5501683834.","after":["lane-dmc-refactor"],"created":"2026-09-01T18:11:53-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T19:09:29-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"1657408c","musts":"0","reviewer":"agent-grok","shoulds":"2"}}
