{"id":"lane-dmc-evidence","parent":"doorbell-missing-claim","ord":"a6","title":"evidence verified #bug","done":"2026-09-01T19:40:41-04:00","desc":"Verified by the orchestrator (2026-09-01 19:40). No visual surface — the evidence is the REGRESSION TEST SEEN RED FIRST (the human's reproduce-red-first law, this lane's first application): the author wrote it, ran it against the unfixed code, and reported it red isolated to the missing claim, then re-verified with the fix reverted; the REVIEWER independently read origin/master and confirmed the old gate would indeed have dropped it (`unfinished(undefined)` is false, so an unmarked mirror was skipped before descending, and the inner gate would have dropped it too). Plus the sibling case pinned beside it (mint-then-graft with no children) so a future widening cannot pass itself off as a regression of this one, and the new structured logging whose derivation lines name the ringing set and now carry each exclusion's REASON. CI 11/11 at fb17222f, no flakes, the watcher having read the #459-overlap legs specifically.","after":["lane-dmc-ci"],"created":"2026-09-01T18:11:53-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T19:40:41-04:00"}
