{"id":"state-pollution","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"aR","title":"PR: e2e runs stop polluting machine state #bug","done":"2026-09-02T10:12:34-04:00","started":"2026-09-02T07:55:38-04:00","worked":8216,"desc":"The harness lets e2e-spawned olai servers write core's machine state into the REAL ~/.local/state/olai (7,320 dead /tmp chat records measured), and nothing prunes records whose directory is gone. Two halves: the harness isolates XDG_STATE_HOME per run (red-first guard test), and core prunes ENOENT-dead records at a ledgered spot. The PR never touches anybody's real state home. SESSION 2 (2026-09-02 ~09:50 ET): session 1 corrupted with raw kimi token spill mid-address — after committing the seven SHOULDs and the master merge locally but before push — killed and respawned fresh in the same worktree.","created":"2026-09-02T07:55:29-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:10-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","brief":"briefs/state-pollution.md","dispatched":"2026-09-02T08:15:00-04:00","from":"the orchestrator's find while showing the human ~/.local/state/olai, 2026-09-02; dispatched on their word","kolu-terminal":"870ddd35","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/b65f604f","odu-worktree":".worktrees/state-pollution","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/469","tier":"ordinary","timings":"implement 1h11m (opencode) · review ~6m 0M/7S (claude-opus) · address ~40m over 2 sessions (kimi corruption between) · ci ~7m 11/11 · merge <1m — TOTAL ~2h17m"}}
