{"id":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"aF","title":"read_subtree hides mirror placements — a board of mirrors reads as empty #feature","done":"2026-09-01T09:27:18-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T23:50:51-04:00","worked":34587,"desc":"Found in real agent use 2026-08-27: the day board's children are all mirror placements, and `read_subtree(day-root)` answers `children: []` — the orchestrator concluded the board had been wiped. The behaviour is documented (\"mirrors are not walked; read a list with read_node's placed\") and the containment/placement distinction is right, but the practical answer to \"what is on this board\" should not be silence: read_subtree should LIST placements at each level (id + target id + target title, unwalked), so a curated list is readable by the read that everything reaches for first. The human's verdict on hearing it: \"wtf is this olai bug\".\n\n**QUEUED (the human, 2026-08-31 ~20:45), first of the night's four lanes**, dispatched when the appliance fold merges — strictly one lane at a time is their pacing. Auto-merge. Still live: the orchestrator walked into this again on 2026-08-31 reading tonight's own day board.","created":"2026-08-27T16:08:27-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T09:27:18-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/mirrors-invisible.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T23:52:00-04:00","from":"the orchestrator's own misread during the 2026-08-27 lanes audit; the human 16:05","kolu-terminal":"abdddf40","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/399501f4","merged":"2026-09-01","odu-worktree":".worktrees/mirrors-invisible","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/454","tier":"ordinary","timings":"implement 8h25m (pi→pi→grok, incl ~6h30m dead session) · refactor 10m23s (grok) · review 2 rounds 15m13s (opus, 1 MUST 2 SHOULD 6 NIT) · address 2 rounds 27m53s · ci 16m52s (11/11 both platforms) · close <1m — TOTAL 9h35m wall, ~3h05m worked"}}
{"id":"lowy-sitting-6","parent":"terminal-door","ord":"a6","title":"The sixth sitting: kolu implementation out of the non-kolu packages #feature","done":"2026-08-27T18:18:19-04:00","desc":"Ratified by the human on 2026-08-27 at about 18:17, after three rounds and five retractions, with the two participating agents swapping sides on the one contested point.\n\n**The shape they agreed on, unanimously:** a new browser-side package `@olai/kolu-ui`, plus a grown `@olai/kolu-client` that also takes over the wire types (contributed to the surface spec by a named spread — the debate's design B), the server-side wiring (as a slice of returned handlers, with the claimants walk injected so the manifest stays clean), a detection entry point, and a test library holding the fake padi daemon and its drivers.\n\nThe connection point is inverted BEFORE anything moves: a `KoluUi` wrapper takes the client whole, and registration is owned by the web package.\n\nThe boundary is enforced by a new assertion in the dependency-check script with ZERO exceptions. On the one contested point — how the chat code probes for kolu — the human ruled for option B: the probe goes through `kolu-client/detect`, which makes the enforcing search unambiguous.\n\nThe conclusion is filed at docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-27.md; the execution rides on pull request #405 as the td-encapsulation item.","created":"2026-08-27T17:32:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T09:18:53-04:00","custom":{"brief":"briefs/debate-kolu-2026-08-26.md","from":"the human 2026-08-27 ~17:35"}}
{"id":"td-encapsulation","parent":"terminal-door","ord":"a7","title":"The encapsulation fold (sitting 6, ratified) #feature","done":"2026-08-28T08:53:05-04:00","desc":"Merged with pull request #405 (squash e5b306bc, 2026-08-28, on the human's approval). Executed exactly as the sixth sitting ratified: the socket inverted in place, the git mv creating @olai/kolu-ui, the detect door (the human's Option B), the wire slice (Design B — after it, kolu-client names no olai package), the join as a returned handlers slice with the vault walk injected, and the fakes/fence/map finish. Both enforcement searches empty at the merged head; the import rule is machine-checked for the first time. Two argued deviations in the pull request body (the geometry harness, recency.ts) plus one type-level improvement (the join's types are parametric, so \"kolu-client cannot read a vault node\" is compiler-checked).","created":"2026-08-27T18:18:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T08:53:05-04:00","custom":{"brief":"briefs/td-encapsulation-fold.md","from":"the sixth sitting, ratified by the human 2026-08-27 ~18:17 (Option B on the chat probe)"}}
{"id":"chat-strip-resumed-agent","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aJ","title":"A resumed subagent never returns to the strip — a running agent with no visible face #feature","done":"2026-08-28T15:43:18-04:00","desc":"MERGED as squash 7dcbf150 (2026-08-28), same day as the human's report. The diagnosis overturned both of the brief's suspects: the strip's membership rule (\"spawned + still running\") was never broken — on a resume nothing on the ACP wire ever said the agent was running again (the spawning call had completed and nothing reopened it); and the × the human clicked was the preview shelf's close, not a dismissal — no dismissal state existed anywhere.\n\nThe fix: the vendored adapter patch (background-tasks-visible) carries a task's second life — a resume reopens the SPAWNING call, and the settle bookends close it; olai adds one clock (ToolEntry.resumed → outSince) so a minute-old resume never reads as running-for-hours; the misleading × is deleted (a shelf closes by its door; a shelf outliving its strip entry closes by the row's door, documented). From review: the siblings invariant — no outing of a call is louder or quieter than its siblings — so a resumed async agent's ending announces exactly as its first did; a pre-existing gap (a spawn's failure line blocking its own refinement) fixed and tested alongside.\n\nGrok reviewed (no MUST; the SHOULD became the invariant). CI: all ten required linux contexts green, mergeStateStatus CLEAN. Evidence: matched pair against a real agent, frame-verified — patched shows the working agent's strip row; stock shows none.","created":"2026-08-28T10:38:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T15:43:30-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/strip-resumed-agent.md","dispatched":"2026-08-28T14:02:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-08-28 — \"I don't see this subagent anymore on ACP chat … is it bug? It used to show up first time, but gone after I clicked the 'x'\"","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/7dcbf150","merged":"2026-08-28T15:44:00-04:00","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/418","terminal":"23b3a947","worktree":".worktrees/strip-resumed-agent"}}
