{"id":"lane-stripres-review","parent":"chat-strip-resumed-agent","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #feature","done":"2026-08-28T15:21:37-04:00","after":["lane-stripres-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-28T14:01:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T15:21:40-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"810b44a7","verdict":"NO MUST — the empty-strip bug closed, bookends hold under an ordered stream, the × deletion clean, the three skips fair. 1 SHOULD: the settle of a reopened call drops backgroundTask, so a resumed async agent's SUCCESS is silent at the transcript bottom and a failed second outing cannot refine its line — reopen-quiet stays, but an ending is an ending: settle should stamp {status, summary}, with tests for both consequences. 2 NITs: previewing.test.ts:54 still names \"the shelf's own dismiss\"; docs/chat.md:328's close-by-the-door slogan fails for a shelf outliving its strip door. PR comment 5456798174."}}
