{"id":"lane-koluev-review-a","parent":"orch-p2a-feed","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #feature","done":"2026-08-28T18:17:55-04:00","after":["lane-koluev-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-28T16:29:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T18:17:58-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"a336b644","verdict":"OBJECT — the shape holds under reading (hold window, same-bucket refresh, mute-on-edit, interval-echo, boot pulse, age-clamp, Dock vocabulary) but a padi link flap produces a transition that should not fire — \"a terminal that left\" is the claim that breaks, and it is the event phase B will wake on. PR comment 5458332941."}}
{"id":"lane-koluev-review-b","parent":"orch-p2a-feed","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus #feature","done":"2026-08-28T18:17:58-04:00","after":["lane-koluev-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-28T16:29:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T18:18:02-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","terminal":"21a40353","verdict":"REQUEST CHANGES. MUST 1: malformed-config lines sink to logDebug while four places promise a console sentence — a vault typo is silent at the default level. MUST 2: `0s` passes the duration grammar and nothing clamps — probed to ~1,900 events/sec, the ring churned every 110ms, from one hand-edited character. SHOULDs: link-flap cleared→remove re-fires every standing hold and re-dates since (converges with grok's MUST); reconfigure re-arms nags from NOW and conflates the two interval guards; watch and mutes can assemble from two different files against the one-file claim. NIT: the ring cap untested in either direction. PR comment 5458315004."}}
