{"id":"lane-koluev-retire","parent":"orch-p2a-feed","ord":"a9","title":"retire terminals #feature","done":"2026-08-29T08:30:27-04:00","after":["lane-koluev-merge"],"created":"2026-08-28T16:29:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T08:30:27-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-p2b-wake","parent":"orch-p2-events","ord":"a1","title":"PR: olai wakes the chat on fleet events #feature","done":"2026-08-31T20:21:31-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T11:15:06-04:00","worked":32785,"desc":"ONE PR (the human, 2026-08-31, collapsing the old two-phase plan): olai delivers fleet events into the chat conversation, and the orchestrator's hand-run Monitor retires in the same landing. **Prototype: [brainstorming/second-doorbell.html](../brainstorming/second-doorbell.html)** · **API sketch: the brainstorm doc's \"second doorbell's door\" section** · DISPATCHED 2026-08-31 ~11:25, claude-opus with ultracode workflows in the prompt, merge the human's.\n\n**THIS IS PLUGIN-KOLU'S FEATURE, whole.** The watcher is already the plugin's (phase A moved with #447); the derivation, the meanings, the digest, the saved events, and the strip's scope control all ship IN the kolu plugin. Core grows only the generic `Deliveries` capability on PluginServices — `scopes()` + write-only `deliver(to, body, {coalesce?})` — and the door is generic or it does not land: no kolu words in core, the fence holds. Kolu disabled = no doorbell, exactly the machine-without-the-tool state.\n\n**The control says the subject, then the filter:** \"kolu: wake on terminal activity · terminals from `<file>`\". The wake is on KOLU TERMINAL ACTIVITY; the served `.olai` file is the FILTER — the kind-`kolu-terminal` values on its un-done nodes, mirrors resolving to targets, so the day board (`orchestrator/lanes.olai`) is the natural filter. **SCOPE IS MANUAL PER CONVERSATION (the human, at dispatch): no serve-level default, no agent-settable op — a fresh or cleared conversation starts with the doorbell OFF until a person picks a file.** A second conversation may filter by a different file and become its own seat.\n\n**How delivery works.** Machine-marked, never as the human, NEVER through the composer — the event rides the wire the way a queued send does; a half-typed draft is untouched. Agent idle → starts a turn. Agent busy → waits its turn behind whatever the human queued first; waiting events coalesce into one summary. A conversation whose session is closed (deploy, closed panel) accumulates its saved events and receives them on reopen as one summary — **and a NEW or cleared conversation subscribes from its own start, inheriting nothing (the human, at dispatch: KISS).** Any agent in the panel works — delivery is a plain message.\n\n**What an event means — derived, never configured. TWO meanings + silence (drift DROPPED, the human at dispatch — the doorbell rings only for claimed terminals):**\n- Claimed by an un-done node in scope, its owning step `doing`, goes quiet → WAKE: a report or a block.\n- Claimed in scope, no step of its lane `doing` → one digest line: lawfully parked.\n- Anything else → silence. An unclaimed terminal is the human's, by default, with no entry anywhere.\n\nThe derivation asks by declared KIND through the licence consult, never key spelling — why this waited for #447 (merged db96ee5c).\n\n**SCOPE ADDED MID-LANE (the human, 2026-08-31 ~15:45, same PR): AVATARS in the chat transcript** — every message names its speaker with a face: the HUMAN through @olai/identity's existing picture ladder, the AGENT through the AgentMark family (group-level, at a speaker's run of messages), and a PLUGIN through its own chrome/manifest contribution (the kolu mark on wake messages — subsuming the kolu-logo steer; odu the second tenant when it delivers). Plus the day's dogfood steers folded into the same round: the pressable claiming-node link (the one clickable thing in a wake), the plain-speech head with the machine body in the fold, the third face. The lane's long span reads honestly against this addition.\n\n**What this removes.** The mutes node in `_olai/Kolu.olai` (the file keeps the watch knobs); the whole mute/unmute ritual; the stale-ignore bug class. **The Monitor retires at the merge**: the orchestrator's wake law is rewritten (no background command, no re-arm, no watch-task bookkeeping) as the retire step's own act — the PR never edits vault files. The proof lives in the PR's tests: idle/busy/no-session delivery, the queue order against a human send, both meanings, against a live board.","after":["orch-p2a-feed"],"created":"2026-08-28T16:29:37-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T20:21:31-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/second-doorbell.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T11:25:00-04:00","kolu-terminal":"27078c86","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/12b3b6ad","merged":"2026-09-01","odu-worktree":".worktrees/second-doorbell","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/450","tier":"design-heavy","timings":"implement 2h17m (opus, ultracode) · refactor + the day's live steers 4h38m · reviews 8m/15m parallel · address incl. heartbeat+fault 1h16m · re-verdicts 5m/4m · final round 10m · ci green twice · close <1m — TOTAL ~8h50m (11:26→20:16)"}}
{"id":"acp-system-prompt","parent":"feat-orch","ord":"aD","title":"PR: ACP chats get a standing system prompt that teaches olai and kolu #feature","todo":true,"desc":"From the human, 2026-08-28, with a screenshot from the kolu-bot instance: an opencode session had to be taught by hand, mid-conversation, that a terminal id goes on a child node as a property, and then that the property key is `terminal` (it had invented `kolu-terminal`). Every fresh ACP session starts ignorant of the house conventions.\n\nTHE PROMPT IS HARDCODED IN OLAI (the human's ruling — no vault-customizable document): built-in text, versioned with the product, teaching what a session needs to be a citizen: the olai MCP conventions (props are short queryable facts and THE VALUE IS THE VALUE; canonical keys — `terminal` bare id, `pr-url` full URL, `agent`, `brief`, `worktree`; marks; notes carry stories, props carry facts; plain words), the kolu MCP (spawn/read/send, the text→settle→Enter submit protocol, ids rotate on restart), and the served vault's layout.\n\nSINCE FILED: pi is the THIRD ACP agent (#422 merged 2026-08-29, with olai/kolu MCP wired through the pinned bridge) — the prompt now serves claude, opencode, AND pi; pi's channel needs the same wire check as opencode's (kimi over pi-acp; `_meta` support unverified there, first-turn injection the safe floor).\n\nDELIVERY — three channels, all verified, layered cheapest-first:\n1. **MCP server `instructions`** (the InitializeResult field, standard MCP): olai's server already ships one — it teaches the tool surface but NOT the conventions; enriching it is nearly free and reaches every client that honors instructions (Claude Code does; others vary — the screenshot's opencode failed despite this channel existing, so it is a layer, not the guarantee).\n2. **`_meta.systemPrompt` at session/new** — Claude adapter ONLY: supported upstream since claude-agent-acp #90/#91 (merged 2025-10-15) and ALREADY IN OLAI'S PIN (acp-agent.js:4845-4918, append-or-override over the claude_code preset), zero patch hunks. NOT available for opencode: olai's own wire spike (agents/opencode.ts:13, 2026-08-21) found `_meta` never appears on any frame of opencode's ACP; and opencode's native rule-file channel (AGENTS.md in cwd) is the vault-document shape the ruling rejects.\n3. **First-turn injection** — the same text as the opening of the session's first prompt: protocol-legal for every agent (NewSessionRequest itself has no prompt field, SDK 1.3.0), the universal floor — and the guaranteed channel for opencode, the agent the motivating screenshot caught failing.","created":"2026-08-28T17:02:54-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T14:54:57-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-pi-agent","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aK","title":"PR: pi joins the ACP chat, via svkozak/pi-acp #feature","done":"2026-08-29T10:14:51-04:00","desc":"The human, 2026-08-28: pi becomes a selectable chat-panel agent through the third-party adapter github.com/svkozak/pi-acp (spiked, pinned, capabilities mirroring the wire). Route A (2026-08-29, the human's pick from the MCP research): the pin's mcp-bridge patch wires session/new's mcpServers through to pi — olai over HTTP, kolu over stdio — verified from the footage (olai_search_nodes and the kolu watch verbs round-tripping in one real session). Route B (the same change upstream, citing pi-acp#38) stays gated on ratification.\n\nMerged 2026-08-29 as PR #422 on the human's conditional word (\"approved once CI green\"), all ten required checks green at cfc12623.","created":"2026-08-28T17:15:06-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:15:05-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/pi-acp.md","dispatched":"2026-08-28T17:16:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/422","terminal":"3e2ed278","tier":"ordinary","worktree":".worktrees/pi-acp"}}
