{"id":"lane-piacp-review-a","parent":"chat-pi-agent","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #feature","done":"2026-08-28T18:19:04-04:00","after":["lane-piacp-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-28T17:15:06-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T18:19:06-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"e31e20da","verdict":"NO MUST — the pin follows the acp-agent.nix pattern with real drift refusals; capability claims verified wire-shaped not README-shaped; recognition edges closed; the accepted-and-ignored mcpServers posture endorsed with chat.md saying the loss; the fromElsewhere null window argued closed (the load-replay door, foreign ids impossible by construction); deferrals match the filed nodes and the unfiled floors are named as floors. SHOULDs/NITs in the comment. PR comment 5458340842."}}
{"id":"lane-piacp-review-b","parent":"chat-pi-agent","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus #feature","done":"2026-08-28T18:19:06-04:00","after":["lane-piacp-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-28T17:15:06-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T18:19:10-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","terminal":"683cf94f","verdict":"CHANGES REQUESTED. MUST: every pi conversation is TOLD it has olai's MCP servers while the shipped pin provably wires none (pi.ts:16, agent.ts:1430) — the accepted-and-ignored posture must not leak a false claim into the conversation. SHOULDs: the prologue arm is never disarmed and the load's disarm lands after the replay it protects (agent.ts:1499); chat.md lacks the prologue posture the body claims (chat.md:33). NITs: both halves of the session/list deferral are off; acp-agent.nix builds two adapters under a one-adapter label. Three findings came from probing the built pin itself. PR comment 5458342301."}}
