{"id":"lane-piacp-mcp-research","parent":"chat-pi-agent","ord":"aA","title":"research: routes to MCP support for pi sessions #feature","done":"2026-08-29T08:18:44-04:00","desc":"Report delivered 2026-08-29 (in the author's terminal): five routes mapped. A — a vendored patch on OUR pi-acp pin wiring session/new's mcpServers through to pi (the adapter already stores them and advertises mcpCapabilities; the patch closes a hole it half-owns, flips the http/sse capability flags, covers olai-over-HTTP and kolu-over-stdio; generated-patch discipline; no permission needed). B — the same change as an upstream pi-acp PR (prior art adjacent to upstream #38), needing ratification. C — pi core grows an MCP client: DEAD, pi's author refuses MCP by design. D — bundling a pi-mcp-adapter in the pin: heavy mismatch (TUI ergonomics, file-based config, big dep tree). E — olai-side proxy: impossible, olai has no channel into pi (only the adapter's spawn reaches it). RECOMMENDATION: A now, B as follow-through — A's code is shape-identical to the upstream PR, so B decays to \"ratify and raise whenever.\"","created":"2026-08-29T08:09:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T08:18:48-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-piacp-mcp-wire","parent":"chat-pi-agent","ord":"aB","title":"route A: the pin's patch wires mcpServers through to pi #feature","done":"2026-08-29T10:14:48-04:00","desc":"The human's pick from the research, 2026-08-29: route A rides the same PR (#422). Route B (the upstream PR, citing svkozak/pi-acp#38) stays gated on ratification.","created":"2026-08-29T08:22:31-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:14:48-04:00"}
{"id":"feed-mutes-footer","parent":"orch-p2-events","ord":"a3","title":"PR: the feed shows its mutes, the wrench opens Kolu.olai, and the vault's own files get a real home #feature","done":"2026-08-29T12:18:06-04:00","desc":"Ruled with the human 2026-08-29 (question tool + expansion): the attention drawer gains a quiet footer — mute count with names drawn live from _olai/Kolu.olai's mutes children, and a wrench that navigates to the Kolu.olai page. The deeper cut in the same PR: the Hidden-outlines setting is deleted; the _olai outlines instead appear as a designed quiet group in the sidebar.\n\nDEEPENED at review time (the human, 2026-08-29 ~10:55, from the PR's second screenshot): the sidebar's vault files — Kolu, Properties, Inbox, AND Trash — nest under ONE special parent node (\"Olai\"), not a flat group. Trash's old top-level entry goes away; it lives inside that parent. One treatment, one parent, the vault's own furniture behind a single door. Lands in the address round, after the reviews fold.","created":"2026-08-29T08:54:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T12:18:06-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/feed-mutes-footer.md","dispatched":"2026-08-29T09:00:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/424","terminal":"4931ecfd","tier":"ordinary","worktree":".worktrees/feed-mutes-footer"}}
