{"id":"lane-fmf-review-a","parent":"feed-mutes-footer","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #feature","done":"2026-08-29T11:00:34-04:00","after":["lane-fmf-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-29T08:54:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T11:00:34-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"6acd3143","verdict":"NO MUST — one walk verified (config.muted + mutes.names off one list), the removal complete with zero survivors, DoorRow accepted as the one mechanism. SHOULD: a present-but-unparseable (or watch/mutes-less) Kolu.olai loses its wrench — the door should survive a broken file the convention can name. NITs: mutesOf encounter-order vs byOrd; the role-less onLeave wrapper. PR comment 5463107435."}}
{"id":"lane-fmf-review-b","parent":"feed-mutes-footer","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus #feature","done":"2026-08-29T11:00:35-04:00","after":["lane-fmf-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-29T08:54:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T11:00:35-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","terminal":"5d290698","verdict":"APPROVE WITH CHANGES, no MUST. SHOULDs: (1) the foot's \"N muted\" counts config entries while foldMutes may silence nobody (ambiguous/inert values) — the reader is told the opposite of what is happening, HACKING.md's surface-errors rule, real work not a one-liner; (2) the mutes cell keeps stale state on a snapshot-less read where pins/inbox reset — stale drawer + wrench on the error report; (3) VaultFile re-spells File's row anatomy (⚠ mark now in three homes). PR comment 5463109444."}}
