{"id":"lane-hup-review","parent":"header-uptime","ord":"a2","title":"review: claude-opus #feature","done":"2026-08-29T10:32:48-04:00","after":["lane-hup-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-29T09:34:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:32:48-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","terminal":"09925ccd","verdict":"REQUEST CHANGES. MUST 1: the reconnect reset the PR is named after cannot happen — a restarted server retires the tab (STALE_PROCESS_CLOSE_CODE; reaching.ts closes the guard), so four doc/header sites + the commit message claim a behavior that does not ship. MUST 2: uptime.test.ts tests only the pure table — the actual changed seam (named.ts's ungated setStarted) is untested. SHOULDs: backoff-free retry spin re-opened per reconnect; a per-second timer held for the tab's life behind a never-closing gate; aria-label on an unfocusable div. PR comment 5462977181."}}
