{"id":"native-timing","ord":"aK","title":"PR: native task timing — started, took, and the ticking row #feature","done":"2026-08-29T16:00:25-04:00","desc":"The human's design (2026-08-29, question tool + the de-hack round): a standalone `started` instant field stamped by set_doing when absent; `took` derived at read time (done − started), never stored; no started → no took. UI always-visible: settled rows wear the quiet ⏱ chip, doing rows tick live pomodoro-style (the uptime chip's local-tick seam). Design: brainstorming/olai-native-timing.md; mock: projects/olai/prototypes/timing-mock.html. Retires the orchestrator's neighbor-subtraction and the typed took prop.\n\n**MERGE AUTHORIZATION STANDING** (the human, 2026-08-29 15:54, \"approved on visual evidence\"): the orchestrator merges without a further ask once the watcher's run posts green at 33b0c52b AND the 17s video frame-verifies against the ruled cases (the stamp, the live tick, the settled chip, re-open keeping the first start, the jump wearing nothing).","created":"2026-08-29T13:03:19-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:30-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","approved":"2026-08-29T15:54:00-04:00","brief":"briefs/native-timing.md","dispatched":"2026-08-29T13:04:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/430","terminal":"c56b6183","tier":"ordinary","timings":"implement 1h22m incl. a compaction (pi) · refactor 19m (pi) · review(∥) 21m (grok+opus) · address+re-verdicts 42m (three MUSTs) · ci 11m (claude-ci) · close <1m — TOTAL 2h55m (13:04→15:59)","worktree":".worktrees/native-timing"}}
