{"id":"lane-lrd-review-b","parent":"landing-reveals-done","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus #feature","done":"2026-08-30T12:40:01-04:00","started":"2026-08-30T12:32:23-04:00","worked":2393,"after":["lane-lrd-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-30T09:11:24-04:00","changed":"2026-08-30T12:40:01-04:00","custom":{"musts":"1","reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","shoulds":"2","terminal":"c5e1651b","verdict":"changes requested — the reveal sound (place-keyed sparing, one door, filter rule all verified) but the census MUST: four of six new numbers do not reproduce (grep bugs — an anchored grep missing quick_capture's mid-line @share-scratch, and five prose @own-scratch counted as tags); opus's verified counts 729/31/463/23, stable at both heads. +2 SHOULDs on the reveal outliving its gates. Comment 5469267465.","verdict-followup":"re-verdict at 7f421e58: census MUST CLEARED (all six numbers reproduce on the entry axis, two independent passes). The two SHOULDs + two NITs STAND — the round touched no client code and neither new scenario reaches the lifetime holes. The phantom fragments adjudicated: they appear in NEITHER review; the author's readout of the comments is the thing to distrust. +1 new NIT (the scenario comment cites filter/reading.ts, which does not exist). Comment 5469416024.","verdict-followup-2":"at 1874d71e: both SHOULDs land (the gate effect is the right shape — no self-conceal loop, safe ordering, file boundary intact; the pane scoping verified both directions), both NITs fixed, the census right. ONE new SHOULD: the landed-side scenario's flip half is vacuous — add a re-landing step before the hidden→shown→hidden round trip; and the census derivation sentence, not its number, needs the honest axis words. Comment 5469548549.","verdict-followup-3":"final at 06eb29bb: Approve, nothing open — the flip half verified by FALSIFICATION (the gate mutation that stayed green last round now fails the scenario); the census re-verified at head, the 732 mistake made unreproducible not merely corrected. Comment 5469639098.","verdict-followup-4":"the router fix at 05797e46: the approval stands — the keyless-popstate discrimination sound, the traversal arm untouched in substance, the paste claim the same mechanism as the reds. Three non-blocking notes (currentKey in the replace branch; the clamped-restore race; the dropped-fragment toTop question). Comment 5469933444."}}
