{"id":"lane-sd-review-b","parent":"orch-p2b-wake","ord":"a3","title":"review: pi #feature","done":"2026-08-31T19:35:23-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T19:28:39-04:00","worked":1347,"after":["lane-sd-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-31T11:15:05-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T19:35:23-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"e7b67f8d","musts":"0","reviewer":"agent-pi","shoulds":"3","verdict":"No MUST. Verified: the four derivation rules are real invariants (post-order claiming walk, territory exclusion, settled-claim skip, per-event and per-delivery re-derivation), each with a test named for the live dogfood shape that broke it; delivery is kolu-free with the composer untouched and ordering structural; the face, the pin-fed mark and the CodeQL fix (true fixpoint, broader refusal, output re-scan, spliced tests) hold. SHOULDs: (1) a renamed/deleted scope file silences that conversation's doorbell forever with no signal on any channel — doorbell.ts:274, Wake.tsx:298 — THE UNSIGNALED RETIREMENT COST, found independently by grok too; (2) a second tenant's deliverable bodies can strand past a boundary when the oldest plugin's batch self-settles — chat.ts:1956-1963, latent today; (3) literal NUL bytes at deliveries.ts:207-208 make the file binary to review tooling — use the \\0 escape. NITs: the undocumented breadth tie-break (doorbell.ts:366), a stale digest quote (docs.md:107).","verdict-followup":"re-verdict at 48630c1f: all three SHOULDs and both NITs genuinely closed — the fault signal is the right mechanism (persisted false→true edge, once, restart-safe; documentAt over set.documents with the empty-file case pinned; sayable-gate for tenant-less serves; heal-silent; delivery-time healed() re-check; the alarm strip with the picker still pressable). ONE REGRESSION, found independently by grok too: SHOULD 3's NUL byte was fixed in deliveries.ts and reintroduced at plugin-kolu/src/doorbell.ts:1066 (makeHeartbeat's keyOf) — grep already answers \"binary file matches\". Two NITs: the fixed bug class (a held offer never asking say) has no counting test; terminalsIn can double-count a terminal written as both prefix and full id."}}
