{"id":"sd-dogfood-log","parent":"orch-p2b-wake","ord":"aC","title":"dogfood log: the old and new doorbells compared","desc":"The human's order at the #450 deploy: run the Monitor beside the doorbell and record every agreement and divergence. Entries 1–8: the FIRST build (34a091d5); 9–18: the FIXED build (34c610a4); 19+: the full-slate head (06182d8b, deployed ~16:25).\n\n1. 14:13 — AGREE. Doorbell 14:13:00, Monitor 14:13:58. Doorbell first.\n2. OBSERVATION: named the claiming LANE as \"the step\" — fixed in 34c610a4.\n3. 14:18–14:19 — MISS: step-level claims never rang — fixed in 34c610a4.\n4. 14:23 — FALSE WAKE for the parked author — fixed in 34c610a4.\n5. 14:30–14:45 — AGREE (correct silence at set_done).\n6–8. STEERS: the third face; no standing set; concise head with the body in the fold.\n9. 15:38 — AGREE on the fixed build: concise WAKE, deepest doing step named.\n10–12. STEERS: the pressable node link; the plugin mark, only the link clickable; plain-speech head.\n13. 15:46 — THE KEY CASE PASSES: a STEP-claimed reviewer rang.\n14. 15:46 + 15:48 — OVER-ATTRIBUTION ×2 (another terminal's claimed step cited as the parked author's).\n15. PROCESS LANDED (approved): dag.olai — orders addressed from the board's prop.\n16. 15:53 — a shared false positive, later CORRECTED as no defect at all: kolu's `waiting` means idle-at-prompt and the watcher was exactly that.\n17. 15:56 — the first DIGEST, with the done-claim leak and the false mark inside it.\n18. 15:57 — STALE AT ARRIVAL: the queued delivery named a closed world; re-derive-at-delivery ruled.\n19. 16:12 — THE FULL SLATE at 06182d8b, every finding with its pin.\n20–21. 16:29–16:31 — the probe's phase 1 passes; the two face corrections sent.\n22. 16:32–16:34 — **THE PROBE PASSES WHOLE**: two claimed agents walked every case — wake on own step, the parked digest under the territory rule, the unclaimed-step wake, silence at a settled claim, silence at lane-done (two Monitor rings, doorbell silent), coalescing, delivery-time honesty.\n23. 17:00 onward — THE DOORBELL RAN THE AFTERNOON'S SUPERVISION, correctly, across three lanes and a server restart: every author report, every reviewer verdict, the parked digests, the silence at each merge. It also caught an orchestrator defect the board could not show — a review step marked `doing` whose terminal was idle, because the reviewer had never been spawned (dag.olai's fourth dispatch law came from it).\n24. 18:20–18:27 — THE REVIEWS: grok and pi, no MUST between them, both verifying the four derivation rules as real invariants with tests named for the live shapes that broke them. **Both found the same gap independently, and it is the one the orchestrator had already named as its condition: a renamed or deleted scope file silences that conversation's doorbell forever, with no signal on any channel, while the control still draws as ON.** pi calls it \"the one unsignaled retirement cost\". Plus: a second tenant's bodies can strand at a boundary (latent until odu delivers), NUL bytes making a file read as binary, a dead helper, two nits.\n25. 18:30 — THE ADDRESS ROUND carries all of it plus **the HEARTBEAT, approved by the human**: a floor on silence rather than a metronome — suppressed by any real delivery, carrying the scope, the set size derived at send time, the last event seen and the watching-since; the period from the watch config's existing `heartbeat` knob; it deliberately starts a turn, since a signal that only lands when the agent is already running proves nothing about the hours it was not. The fault signal and the heartbeat stay distinct sentences: \"alive but cannot watch what you asked\" is not a heartbeat with bad news.\n\n**WHAT REMAINS BEFORE THE MONITOR RETIRES:** the address round, both re-verdicts, CI at the final head, the human's review and merge. Then the retire step rewrites the wake law and the Monitor stops — with the fault signal and the heartbeat making silence legible, which was the whole of the orchestrator's objection.","created":"2026-08-31T14:15:03-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:55:58-04:00"}
{"id":"timing-chip-hover","parent":"feat-tasks","ord":"a8","title":"PR: the timing chip's hover shows every round #feature","done":"2026-08-31T19:23:52-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T15:23:53-04:00","worked":14399,"desc":"Today the chip's hover says only \"under way since <instant>\" — the current round's start. Wanted: the chip stays its concise self, and the HOVER carries the breakdown — each doing-round's span in order, the worked total (rounds summed, pauses excluded), and the wall span (first start → last settle, or → now while running). Single-round steps read naturally (\"round 1, under way since …\"); multi-round steps finally show what #435's counting already knows. The same concise-face-details-on-hover principle the human ruled for the doorbell's wake messages, applied to the timing chip.\n\nDISPATCH RULED (the human, 2026-08-31): goes out at the fixed #450 deploy, and DOUBLES AS THE DOORBELL PROBE — the lane's own lifecycle exercises the whole wake flow (silent while working, a WAKE naming the deepest doing step at the report, a step-claimed reviewer ringing, the parked author drawing a digest, silence at the merge), and that run is the Monitor's retirement evidence. Author: opencode — its turn in the kimi alternation, and its first compaction-ledger entries.","created":"2026-08-31T15:19:12-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T19:23:52-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","brief":"briefs/timing-chip-hover.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T15:24:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-08-31 ~15:20, hovering a live chip; dispatch ruled at ~15:25 — at the fixed #450 deploy, as THE PROBE LANE","kolu-terminal":"ceb736d4","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/e6bcc586","merged":"2026-08-31","odu-worktree":".worktrees/timing-chip-hover","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/452","tier":"ordinary","timings":"implement 2h23m (opencode) · refactor 24m · reviews 9m×2 parallel · address 10m · re-verdicts 2m/4m · short round 7m · ci 5m32s 11/11 · close <1m — TOTAL ~4h (15:24→19:24)"}}
