{"id":"lane-tch-review-a","parent":"timing-chip-hover","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #feature","done":"2026-08-31T18:46:17-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T18:43:07-04:00","worked":1314,"after":["lane-tch-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-31T15:23:53-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T18:46:17-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"0ae7f74c","musts":"0","reviewer":"agent-grok","shoulds":"1","verdict":"No MUST. SHOULD at Tip.tsx:108 — the new vertical clamp is an untested viewport-floor pin that EVERY tip inherits, not the flip-over-the-anchor the body describes (opus found the same layer independently). NIT at outline_tree_steps.ts:327 — the hover read drops the exactly-one-tip count that navigation_steps.ts treats as the doubled-tooltip catch. Comment 5485658967.","verdict-followup":"re-verdict at 424016cb: both closed — no MUST, no remaining SHOULD, no remaining NIT. Comment 5485782538."}}
{"id":"lane-tch-review-b","parent":"timing-chip-hover","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus #feature","done":"2026-08-31T18:48:39-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T18:43:07-04:00","worked":1531,"after":["lane-tch-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-31T15:23:53-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T18:48:39-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"5c87b2c8","musts":"0","reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","shoulds":"5","verdict":"No MUST. Verified: the Tip upgrades are general (no prop, no knob, no caller contract), the e2e mints no vocabulary and is not vacuous, the evidence wrote only a gitignored copy (zero ev- rows in the live vault) and two shots show verbatim what the unit tables pin. Five findings: (1) the new vertical clamp is three-number arithmetic in the component against tip.ts's own charter — zero tests where clampedLeft has four, and it drops the header floor clampedTop exists to enforce; (2) the body's \"multi-line-only\" claim is wrong — the box is ~26px, so it re-places every one-line tip anchored in the last ~38px; (3) the sr-only copy sits inside the chip, so `is ticking`'s innerText assertion no longer proves the face moved; (4) chip.hover() sits outside the poll — the same race this PR's own evidence needed a retry for; (5) THE WALL SPAN IS UNDERIVABLE (started is restamped per round) so the brief's third deliverable is undelivered and unrecorded — it belongs under ## Deferrals or the model must keep the first start.","verdict-followup":"re-verdict at 424016cb: all five closed and verified (the clamp moved with its sibling's tests and floor; the multi-line claim gone from comment and body with the one-line lift tested; the sr-only copy a sibling so innerText proves the face again — firstElementChild still the chip, sr-only adds no box; hover inside the poll, carrying the exactly-one-tip count which also closes grok's NIT; the wall span under Deferrals with cause, price and whose decision). NEW SHOULD: outline_tree_steps.ts:330 — the re-hover only re-opens the tip when the chip moved under the pointer, because Tip listens to onMouseEnter only; the saatchi retry knew this and moved the mouse away first, the step should too. 4 NITs: liftedTop's floor leg drops TIP_GAP (and MARGIN with no bar), MARGIN's export is vestigial, place writes the drawn position back into the ask on both axes, the anchor's first-child contract is order-dependent."}}
