{"id":"chat-adapter-bump","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aP","title":"PR: bump the pinned chat adapter #feature","done":"2026-09-01T11:46:18-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T08:22:23-04:00","worked":12235,"desc":"The pinned claude-agent-acp sits at 0.66.0 while the current release is 0.70.0, and the pin now carries a local patch (`acp/patches/`, from #365 — the background-task lifetimes the chat panel draws its clocks and deaths from). A bump check has been owed since the 2026-08-24 roadmap review and nothing has asked for one since.\n\n**THE HUMAN'S RULING AT DISPATCH (2026-08-31 ~20:45): BUMP ONLY, AND SAY WHAT OPENED.** Move the pin, re-apply the local patch — or RETIRE it, if upstream has fixed the thing it works around, which is a result rather than a failure — prove the panel still works, and name in the PR body which blocked items the new version unblocks. The two things waiting on this bump, `chat-rewind` (no conversation rewind yet) and `upstream-steer-after-queued-hang` (#366's interrupt guard comes off when issue #1039 is fixed), are NOT in this PR: each becomes its own lane with its own review. Naming them is the deliverable; taking them is not, and their absence is not a deferral.\n\n**Merge is the human's** — they read it in the morning. The chat panel is the surface they steer the fleet through, so a green bump still waits for a person.\n\nSecond in the overnight queue, behind the odu pair, dispatched when that lane merges.","see":["chat-rewind","upstream-steer-after-queued-hang"],"created":"2026-08-31T20:48:39-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T11:46:18-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/chat-adapter-bump.md","dispatched":"2026-09-01T08:19:00-04:00","kolu-terminal":"7b6ab06f","merge":"merge-human","odu-worktree":".worktrees/chat-adapter-bump","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/456","tier":"design-heavy","timings":"implement 74m + refactor 27m (claude-opus) · reviews pi 47m / grok 29m · address 17m · merge-master 7m + ci 10m (grok, post-switch) · dispatch→merge 3h26m"}}
{"id":"lane-mi-implement","parent":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR #feature","done":"2026-09-01T08:15:46-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T23:50:51-04:00","worked":30295,"desc":"TWO DEAD SESSIONS, THEN A CHANGE OF AGENT. The Juspay kimi pool went out and stayed out:\n\n- pi #1 (83892b49) died 2026-09-01 04:27 UTC on `Retry failed after 3 attempts: Connection error`, implementation finished, nothing committed. The lane then sat dead six and a half hours — the doorbell's forty nags reached the conversation in one batch at 10:57 rather than as sent.\n- pi #2 (0117e874) resumed in the same worktree at 10:58, re-read the diff, and died the same way at ~11:18, including on an explicit manual retry.\n\nNot the host: `api.github.com` answers 200 from this machine, and gh works. Not the API key either — the JUSPAY_API_KEY reminder puts its expiry at ~2026-11-24. It is the pool, which pi and opencode SHARE, so opencode is not a fallback.\n\n**Handed to grok (abdddf40) in the same worktree on standing authority**, not on a fresh ruling: the choosing rule already says grok takes the work when both kimi agents are occupied, THE POOL IS DOWN, or the work is grok-shaped. The ten modified files from pi #1 are still on disk, uncommitted; grok was told to read the diff and judge it rather than inherit it. One open question grok must resolve: pi #2's `nix build .#olai` ended with `Reason: 1 dependency failed` beside an output path, which may be a real break in the change or an unrelated cache miss.","created":"2026-08-31T21:03:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T08:15:46-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-mi-refactor","parent":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","ord":"a1","title":"refactor passes #feature","done":"2026-09-01T08:26:09-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T08:15:46-04:00","worked":623,"after":["lane-mi-implement"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T08:26:09-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-mi-review-a","parent":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #feature","cancelled":"2026-09-01T08:00:54-04:00","desc":"CANCELLED because grok became the author: an author never reviews its own lane. This is an ordinary-tier lane, so the tier rule's pairing is a commodity author with claude-opus reviewing — one review step, which is `lane-mi-review-b`. The two-reviewer shape here only existed because the lane was kimi-authored, and it is not any more.","after":["lane-mi-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T08:00:55-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok"}}
{"id":"lane-mi-review-b","parent":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus #feature","done":"2026-09-01T09:02:00-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T08:55:27-04:00","worked":913,"desc":"Two rounds, both by claude-opus in a split of the author's terminal.\n\n**Round 1 at 675bbf4c:** approve with 1 MUST, 2 SHOULD, 3 NIT. The MUST was the one that earned the seat — a `placed` entry was a FULL situated row regardless of `fields`, whole `custom` map included, so a two-field walk over a day board answered exactly the place-and-ancestry the dial exists to drop. The second finding that mattered: the file arm left the same silence one level up, with a recovery route that closed on itself.\n\n**Round 2 at a85130d6:** approve, 3 NIT. It verified the two things the fix itself could have broken and found both sound for the right reasons — the `read_node`/`read_subtree` agreement holds because it is still ONE producer (`placedAmong`), and the union decode cannot mis-arm because `Projected` cannot mint `file`/`line`/`path`. The new file-arm key is pinned four ways, including the fixture-reach test that closes declared-but-never-produced and produced-but-never-declared in one stroke.\n\nThe surviving NITs are a type-precision call (`shows: Union([Found, Projected])` widens three reads that can never produce the second arm), one cross-reference clause that did not get the same edit as the description it points at, and a double walk of the file's top level one line apart.","after":["lane-mi-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T09:02:00-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"2e2d2fc3","musts":"1","reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","shoulds":"2"}}
