{"id":"lane-mi-evidence","parent":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","ord":"a7","title":"evidence verified #feature","done":"2026-09-01T09:26:21-04:00","desc":"VERIFIED as proof rather than a photograph — this lane changes an MCP read shape and has no visual face. What stands as evidence: `an_external_agent.feature` 21/21 against the nix binary, including the new scenario where an agent writes a placement at the top of `house.olai` and reads the whole outline back — the scenario that used to DEMONSTRATE the hole now demonstrates it closed. The reviewer independently confirmed the file-arm key is pinned four ways, the load-bearing one closing declared-but-never-produced and produced-but-never-declared in a single assertion. CI 11/11 both platforms at a6a05877.","after":["lane-mi-ci"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T09:26:21-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-mi-deferrals","parent":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","ord":"a8","title":"deferrals ruled #human #feature","done":"2026-09-01T09:26:21-04:00","desc":"GATE CLEAR: `## Deferrals` reads `No deferrals.` across all three rounds — implement, address, and the nit round. Nothing was filed as a follow-up, and the one finding that could have become a deferral (the file arm answering `roots: []` for an all-mirror outline) was fixed in the lane rather than deferred, on the orchestrator's instruction that shipping without it would ship half the lane's own fix.","after":["lane-mi-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:03:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T09:26:21-04:00"}
