{"id":"lane-cab-review-a","parent":"chat-adapter-bump","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #feature","done":"2026-09-01T11:26:44-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T11:08:48-04:00","worked":1760,"desc":"Approve, and the review is a verification rather than a reading — which is what a PR made of claims needs. It spent its one probe on the two published tarballs, because claims about the UNPATCHED pin cannot be settled from this tree.\n\nWhat it confirmed by measurement: the re-anchored patch's added lines are byte-identical to the reviewed ones **436 of 436**, removed 1 of 1, with the only non-header drift being three trailing context lines on the one hunk that had to move — so a reviewed patch was not silently replaced by an unreviewed one. 0.70.0 really does insert a `SessionFailureController` between the two anchors. The 0.66→0.70 diff is 1572 lines and contains no line of the task vocabulary. Upstream PR #941 is still open with 0 reviews.\n\nIt also checked the two standing-alone survivals were the RIGHT checks rather than merely claimed — tracing why a dropped `message.timestamp` would show as `sawClear` without `at` and no link, which is the silent break the README warns about.\n\nAnd it added the reason the Monitor negative is not a lucky miss: the adapter does not special-case Monitor versus Bash at settlement, but one layer down a Monitor WAKES THE MODEL per event while a background Bash does not until it dies. So widening the latch to \"any task\" would take the interrupt away from conversations that never needed to lose it.\n\nRound 2 at 16bac3d4 (the narrow re-verdict the orchestrator asked for — does any sentence the address round ADDED assert something untrue): **approve** — no fifth false claim; the chat.md citation sentence it had flagged now admits that file cites the patches README at the wire-carries paragraph, which it does. Posted 2026-09-01 15:14Z as a reply on the c4e0bf5e thread.","after":["lane-cab-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-31T21:04:20-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T11:26:44-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"d86a938a","musts":"0","reviewer":"agent-grok","shoulds":"2"}}
