{"id":"odu-checkout-targeting","parent":"orch-odu","ord":"a3","title":"PR: odu MCP targets a checkout #upstream #feature","done":"2026-09-01T15:22:48-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T13:13:21-04:00","worked":7767,"desc":"The enabler the olai doorbell lane specified at its stop-and-ask (pi, 2026-09-01 ~13:10): (1) a per-call `checkout` argument on odu mcp's bespoke tools, default process.cwd() for back-compat; (2) run-spawned coordinators outlive the MCP server (today `killRuns()` on close kills them — an olai restart would kill CI runs); (3) the .ci log-path rule exported through @odu/run-client so consumers never re-spell it. The olai lane pins this PR's head during development; the pin moves to the merge commit before the olai PR merges (the odu#94 → olai#433 pattern).\n\n**Seat notes:** opencode takes the kimi seat (the alternation — pi is occupied authoring the consumer lane); grok reviews in claude-opus's stead while the weekly limit holds (the tier rule wants opus on an ordinary lane — deviation for the human's veto, same as today's standing substitutions).","created":"2026-09-01T13:13:21-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T15:22:48-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","brief":"briefs/odu-checkout-targeting.md","dispatched":"2026-09-01T13:18:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-09-01: odu PRs dispatch separately in parallel; the olai PR uses the odu PR directly","kolu-terminal":"e767b246","merge":"merge-human","odu-worktree":".worktrees/checkout-targeting","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/odu/pull/97","tier":"ordinary","timings":"implement 65m + refactor 14m + address 18m (opencode) · review grok 15m over 2 rounds · ci both platforms 9m (grok) · merge-master skipped · dispatch→merge 2h4m"}}
