{"id":"lane-nap-review-a","parent":"node-agents-p1","ord":"a2","title":"review: pi #feature","done":"2026-09-01T21:53:02-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T21:45:59-04:00","worked":2345,"desc":"pi at ca8c69a8: **request changes — 2 MUST, 3 SHOULD, 2 NIT**, both MUSTs in the keystone (the subtree-memory teaching). (1) chat.ts:1708 — teaching is ADDRESSED outside `opening.withPermit` but DELIVERED inside it: a send parked while another tab switches sessions lands session X's contract into Y's transcript and durably marks X's binding taught though X never heard it — the exact failure the Teaching interface's own comment claims to prevent, entered through the other door; teaching() is pure so a one-line move fixes it. (2) The once-per-session rule is UNTESTED at the implementing layer — nothing builds `make` with binding/charge, the rule lives in chat.ts's send path and would stay green if INVERTED, and the wire's `taught` field (surface/agents.ts:90) exists solely so a scenario can assert second-message silence, which node_agents.feature does not contain. SHOULDs: the false live-pickup claim at chat.ts:1017 (hand-edits land at restart, docs don't say so); the said.at write-time stamp that lies after resume (chat.ts:1111); three package READMEs a row stale each. Comment 5501624304.","after":["lane-nap-refactor"],"created":"2026-09-01T17:08:41-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T21:53:02-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"296a499a","musts":"2","reviewer":"agent-pi","shoulds":"5"}}
