{"id":"feat-state-in-vault","parent":"feat-chat","ord":"aQ","title":"PR: machine state moves into the vault #feature","todo":true,"desc":"The human's direction, 2026-09-02 (from reading ~/.local/state/olai/ together): the state home's tenants become rows in claimed _olai files — visible, pressable, one config story. The rendered shape they approved: _olai/Chat.olai holds `chat` (the panel's one reopen row: agent/session/model props) and `heard` (one row per node agent: node/session/taught/said, the node prop pressable, the session drawn with the live pill — which makes boarding `said` history-only); the wake picks land as `wake scopes` rows under each plugin's own file (_olai/Kolu.olai, a new _olai/Odu.olai); olai-plugin-xyne-spaces' thread map under _olai/Spaces.olai.\n\nDESIGN FIRST — three questions rule the scope before any dispatch:\n1. CHURN: `chat` rewrites per panel-open and `heard` per turn; with auto-push on that is a vault commit per turn. Needs an answer (a volatile-write lane that batches? heard staying machine-side? said dropped since the pill shows it live?).\n2. PER-MACHINE FACTS: session ids mean nothing on another machine — dead rows there, or a machine key on each row.\n3. PRIVACY: `said` lines land in git history forever.\nThe wake picks are the clean first slice — they change only on a human decision, exactly a board fact.","created":"2026-09-02T07:54:13-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-09-02, ruling direction after the state-home walkthrough"}}
