{"id":"doorbell-settle-is-socket-death","parent":"orch-odu","ord":"a8","title":"PR: the CI status plugin reads \"settled\" from the run, not the socket #feature","done":"2026-09-03T06:32:42-04:00","started":"2026-09-02T21:23:16-04:00","worked":32966,"desc":"Found 2026-09-02 20:20–20:32 ET: two green runs (odu#98 at 20:21, olai#474's run 4 at 20:26) reached the chat as \"settled\" only at 20:32, the moment their lingering coordinators were cancelled. olai-plugin-odu's watcher (packages/odu-client/src/runs.ts: \"THE RUN SETTLED — the socket is gone\") treats the coordinator's socket closing as the run settling. That signal was right before odu's `linger` option existed; with `linger` the coordinator keeps the socket open on purpose after the run has settled (so one node can be re-run), and the plugin has nothing else to read — so a finished run is reported up to the idle reap (~30 min) late. THE FIX: read the run's own settlement — the coordinator answers it over the same socket, and odu's ledger stamps `finishedAt` — and say \"settled\" on that; the socket's death stays the signal for a run that died. The human's word (20:45 ET): this is a bug, not a usage rule. QUEUED by the human (~20:48 ET) after the plugin-directories lane — the `after` edge points at its merge.","after":["lane-pd-merge"],"see":["odu-run-dies-with-mcp-host"],"created":"2026-09-02T20:37:18-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T06:32:42-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","brief":"briefs/settle-from-the-run.md","dispatched":"2026-09-03T21:24:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-09-02 ~20:45 ET, on the orchestrator's RCA of the silent settles","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/4824d84b","merged":"2026-09-03","odu-worktree":".worktrees/settle-from-the-run","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/481","tier":"ordinary","timings":"implement 32m red-first (opencode) · refactor 12m27s · review 9m19s + re-verdict 2m (claude-opus) · address 11m24s + notes 4m · ci 6m 12/12 · parked overnight ~7h30m on the human's word · merge <1m — TOTAL ~9h (21:24 → 06:31 ET), ~1h15m worked"}}
