{"id":"pictures-on-nodes","ord":"aM","title":"Pictures on nodes","desc":"**TL;DR.** A picture is a FACT OF A NODE, not markdown in its note: paste, drop or pick a picture onto a row and the row draws it, the way Workflowy does. Four PRs in order below; the human's order 2026-09-03 ~11:35 ET (\\\"forget markdown\\\"), after researching Workflowy.\n\n**How Workflowy does it (researched 2026-09-03, sources in the item notes).** A bullet holds text AND one file; the file is not a child, not a link in the text, not a separate node type. Gestures: paste from the clipboard, drag a file onto the bullet, the bullet menu's \\\"Upload file\\\" and a slash command; on the phone, swipe the bullet, then \\\"Upload file\\\" (the only gesture a phone has). The picture renders inline in the bullet at once, with a drag handle to resize, a settings toggle for the default thumbnail size (big or small), full-screen on click, open-original and download icons, and delete with a confirmation. The data model, per the community client, is a `file` object on the node: fileName, fileType (MIME), imageOriginalWidth, imageOriginalHeight, and signed URLs for the original and a resized preview. Bytes live on Workflowy's servers (free: 100 MB total; Pro: 5 GB per file; 15 files a minute for everyone). The outline export formats do not document how a picture is represented; a separate files export zips every file. Sources: https://workflowy.com/help/files-images/ , https://blog.workflowy.com/files-and-images-capture-organize-and-share-all-your-documents/ , https://github.com/karelklima/workflowy , https://blog.workflowy.com/files-export/ .\n\n**Contrast.** Logseq and Obsidian write the file into the vault (an `assets/` folder; the note's own folder or a configured attachment folder) and put a markdown or wiki-link reference into the text. Notion stores a block with a signed, expiring S3 URL. Olai takes Workflowy's shape (a fact on the node) with Logseq's storage (a file in the vault, under git).\n\n**What olai already has (grounded on master 2026-09-03).** The chat's paste path (#87): one policy module for the cap, the 3 MiB chunk and the picture allowlist (`packages/surface/src/attach.ts`), a chunked `chat.attach` procedure, the browser's chunk loop behind three listeners, and a receiver with the realpath fence, collision suffix and name cut (`packages/chat/src/attachments.ts`), which stores in a tmp dir OUTSIDE the vault and discards it on purpose. The `/media/<path>` route serves any picture under the served root, fenced to it. The store already walks picture files (the image kind is registered, bytes not kept). The commit panel lists any new file as dirty for a person to tick; nothing commits on its own. `_olai/` is the one olai-owned directory precedent (Trash, Inbox, Pins).\n\n**Decisions taken here, for the human to overrule.** (1) Bytes go under `_olai/files/`, one folder, vault-wide, next to the other olai-owned files. (2) One picture per node, as Workflowy; more is a later item. (3) The fact is a property on the node, `picture`, holding the vault-relative path, so `set_prop` on the MCP can attach one and `search_nodes prop:picture` finds them all; no new field in the format. (4) Delete takes the property off; the file stays on disk until the commit panel or a later sweep deals with it.","created":"2026-09-03T11:33:41-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:30-04:00"}
{"id":"picture-lands","parent":"pictures-on-nodes","ord":"a0","title":"PR: a picture lands in the vault #feature","todo":true,"desc":"The receptacle. A chunked procedure beside `chat.attach` (not a widening of it: the chat's answer is a tmp path that dies with the conversation, this one's is a vault path that lives under git) that writes a picture under `_olai/files/` with the name sanitised, cut by bytes and suffixed on collision, the same 50 MB cap re-checked against the total, the same realpath fence against the served root, and the same policy module for the allowlist and the refusal wording. Reuses the receiver's logic from `packages/chat/src/attachments.ts` with a \"where\" instead of a tmp dir. Answers `{path, name}`. Done means: a unit test of the fence and the cap against the vault root; the store lists the file after it lands; the commit panel shows it dirty. Bans: no new copy of the chunk arithmetic; nothing written outside `_olai/files/`; no auto-commit.","created":"2026-09-03T11:33:41-04:00","custom":{"merge":"merge-human","tier":"ordinary"}}
{"id":"picture-on-node","parent":"pictures-on-nodes","ord":"a1","title":"PR: a node carries a picture and the row draws it #feature","todo":true,"desc":"The fact and the face. A node's `picture` property holds a vault-relative path; the row draws the picture inline under the title as a thumbnail, full size on click, through the existing `/media/<path>` route; a missing file draws the undrawn-picture placeholder the markdown renderer already has. A row menu entry removes it (takes the property off; the bytes stay until dealt with). The MCP needs nothing new to attach one (`set_prop picture`), and `read_node` answers the path as it answers any property. Done means: a picture draws in the outline, in a mirror of the node, and in the day board; keyboard focus and editing of the title are unchanged with a picture under it; an e2e scenario sets the property on a node and sees the image drawn. Bans: no markdown in the note; no second allowlist; the browser never builds the media path itself outside `mediaHref`.","after":["picture-lands"],"created":"2026-09-03T11:33:41-04:00","custom":{"merge":"merge-human","tier":"design-heavy"}}
{"id":"picture-gestures","parent":"pictures-on-nodes","ord":"a2","title":"PR: paste, drop and pick a picture onto a row #feature","todo":true,"desc":"The three gestures the composer already has, on a row: paste from the clipboard while the row is focused, drag a file onto the row, and a row-menu \"Add a picture\" that opens the file picker (the one gesture a phone has, as Workflowy's swipe-then-upload). One function behind three listeners, as in `packages/web/src/client/chat/Composer.tsx` and `DropTarget.tsx`; upload through the receptacle, then `apply` sets `picture` on the node with the concurrency guard. A refusal (an SVG, too big) is said out loud in the row, before any upload. Done means: an e2e scenario pastes a picture onto a row and sees it drawn and the file under `_olai/files/`; a second paste replaces the picture. Bans: no upload before the gate; no gesture on the title input that steals plain-text paste.","after":["picture-on-node"],"created":"2026-09-03T11:33:41-04:00","custom":{"merge":"merge-human","tier":"ordinary"}}
{"id":"picture-to-agent","parent":"pictures-on-nodes","ord":"a3","title":"PR: the agent sees a node's picture #feature","todo":true,"desc":"When a node with a picture is in the chat's context (selected, or named), the agent is told the picture's absolute path as text, exactly as the chat's own attachments are (\"Attached image: <path>\"), and Claude Code reads the file itself; no base64 in the prompt. Done means: a scripted-agent e2e scenario opens the path it was given and reports the byte count. Bans: no dependency on ACP image content blocks (a later change to one function, as #87 argued).","after":["picture-on-node"],"created":"2026-09-03T11:33:41-04:00","custom":{"merge":"merge-human","tier":"ordinary"}}
{"id":"dispatch-is-one-op","parent":"feat-orch","ord":"aJ","title":"PR: a dispatch is one op, so it cannot be half-done #feature","todo":true,"desc":"**Why, from three failures in one day (2026-09-03).** The orchestrator launched CI on both platforms when the ruling says olai launches linux-only; spawned an author with a bare `claude` instead of the roster row's `claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions`, so it ran on the wrong model without YOLO; and dispatched two lanes without the `kolu-terminal` prop, which is the doorbell's only claim key, so both lanes were invisible to the instrument the orchestrator depends on.\n\n**One cause.** A dispatch today is six independent writes — create the terminal, write six props, flip the mark, mint the day mirror, write the brief, send the prompt — and the values for them live in three different law nodes: the roster row holds the literal command, the lanes conventions hold the six props, ci-venue holds the platforms. The node actually read at the moment of acting (`dag-pr-implement`) describes the act in prose and carries pointers to all three, not one literal value. Prose reconstructs from memory; values do not. Any of the six writes can be forgotten, and three were.\n\n**The fix: make it unspellable to do half.** One op on the roadmap item — give it the agent id, the brief path and the worktree name — that reads the roster row for the literal command, creates the toplevel kolu terminal with it, writes every prop including `kolu-terminal` from the terminal it just created, flips the item and the implement step to doing, and mints the day mirror. It refuses when an input is missing or the roster row has no command, and it is atomic: no terminal without props, no props without a terminal.\n\n**Not in scope:** sending the prompt (the brief's content is a judgement, and a wrong prompt is not the failure this fixes) and choosing the agent (the tier rule stays the orchestrator's reading).","created":"2026-09-03T12:23:38-04:00","custom":{"merge":"merge-human","tier":"design-heavy"}}
{"id":"doorbell-unclaimed-lane","parent":"feat-orch","ord":"aK","title":"PR: the doorbell says when a working lane has no terminal, and when a terminal has no lane #feature","todo":true,"desc":"The cheap half of the same fix as `dispatch-is-one-op`, and it uses the instrument that already exists. olai-plugin-kolu walks the un-done nodes of the scoped board to find terminals claimed by a `kolu-terminal` prop. Give it the two inverses, each said ONCE and not nagged:\n\n- **A working lane with no terminal.** A lane whose implement (or any) step is `doing` while its parent node carries no `kolu-terminal` is not dispatched, it is lost: nothing will ever wake the conversation about it. Two lanes were in that state today for half an hour each and nothing said so.\n- **A terminal with no lane.** A live terminal whose cwd is under a repo's `.worktrees/` that no un-done lane claims — either the dispatch half-failed or the lane closed without retiring it.\n\nBoth are read off the same walk the doorbell already does, so the cost is one pass over nodes it has in hand. Neither is a nag: they are said when the condition appears and again only if it appears again. The existing rule that the plugin never reads a step's meaning is untouched: this reads whether a prop is PRESENT, not what the board means by it.","see":["dispatch-is-one-op"],"created":"2026-09-03T12:23:46-04:00","custom":{"merge":"merge-auto","tier":"ordinary"}}
{"id":"caret-flows","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"a9","title":"PR: the caret flows — arrows across rows, blank bullets, note clicks, split stays put #feature","done":"2026-09-04T14:31:48-04:00","started":"2026-09-03T12:56:08-04:00","worked":92140,"desc":"Dispatched by the human 2026-09-03 ~13:00 ET: \"dispatch all of the following (one PR) to Opencode now (claude reviewer)\". Four behaviours, one PR, in their own words:\n\n1. **Arrow keys flow through the outline.** Left at the start of a line lands at the end of the line above; Right at the end goes to the start of the line below. Up and Down keep your column instead of jumping to the end.\n2. **Blank lines behave like bullets.** After Enter Enter Enter you can Tab a blank in, Shift+Tab it out, and move it, before typing anything.\n3. **Click a note, get a caret.** One click on a note's preview puts the caret where you clicked, instead of expanding it first and needing a second click.\n4. **Enter mid-line stays put.** Splitting a bullet that has children leaves the new half right under it, not at the bottom of the subtree.\n\nThis is most of Layer B of `brainstorming/editing-ux-vs-workflowy.md`, minus the optimistic-position piece (a local indent that snaps back on refusal), which is NOT in the lane. It answers that document's problem headings A4, B3, B5 and D1.\n\nTWO RULINGS THE BRIEF CARRIES so the author does not chase them: A2 is rejected (no guessing a row from a bare keystroke) and A8 is withdrawn as false (the edit face never truncates; title wrapping is a reading question, not a defect).\n\nMERGE POLICY NOT STATED by the human at dispatch; the orchestrator set `merge-human` because the lane touches the editor's core seam. Say the word to make it auto.\n\nGrounded before dispatch: item 3's plumbing half exists (the editor's `open` already takes a position for either field) but its one caller passes none, and #475's click-to-offset code is title-only by construction, so a wrapped note needs line-aware hit-testing of its own. Item 4 is the same \"add after the subtree\" shape #477 fixed for Enter at column 0.","see":["blank-drafts","missing-chords"],"created":"2026-09-03T12:56:08-04:00","changed":"2026-09-04T14:31:49-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","brief":"briefs/caret-flows.md","dispatched":"2026-09-03T13:02:00-04:00","kolu-terminal":"f1a02d20","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/4d5578c4","odu-worktree":".worktrees/caret-flows","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/493","tier":"design-heavy"}}
