{"id":"lane-cf-ci","parent":"caret-flows","ord":"a5","title":"CI green at head #feature","done":"2026-09-04T14:31:48-04:00","desc":"⛔ The human's hold on odu runs stands (2026-09-03 ~17:12 ET), and the orchestrator has launched nothing. A run WAS started by someone else: `check 08670c1#1`, live in the lane's worktree, first red reported 13:44 ET.\n\n**THE RED, read by the orchestrator 13:47 ET.** `e2e[3-of-6]@x86_64-linux`, 46/49 nodes green at the time of the report; within that shard 183 of 184 scenarios pass. The one failure is `keyboard_editing.feature:295`, \"Alt+Shift+Up does not jump the parked blanks the arrows stop on\" — three Enters from the title of \"knobs\", then Alt+Shift+Up, and the draft is expected immediately above the title of \"kitchen-herbs\" rather than below its subtree. It times out after 15s at `editing_steps.ts:626`.\n\nThat is the scenario grok's MUST asked for. Later commits on this branch also touched the same behaviour (\"Tab is one level, never the flight's depth — and blanks are lines to the move keys too\"), so the fix and its pin may have drifted apart.\n\n**THE AUTHOR IS DEAD.** Terminal f1a02d20 shows a bare bash prompt with no agent; opencode exited some time between 12:53 and 13:30 ET, having committed up to 08670c1a first. Per the roster an opencode session does not resume — the remedy is a fresh start in the same worktree with a pointer to where it left off. Not restarted: awaiting the human's word.","after":["lane-cf-merge-master","lane-cf-address","lane-cf-video"],"created":"2026-09-03T12:56:08-04:00","changed":"2026-09-04T14:31:48-04:00"}
