{"id":"mcp-read-batch","ord":"b04","title":"MCP reads need batching too: a whole outline in one call, and notes returned with search hits #infra","done":"2026-08-21T14:57:42-04:00","desc":"From the orchestrator's audit of its own usage (2026-08-21): the write side already refuses to loop — add_node takes children three levels deep with waitsOn, see and props; update writes several fields of one node; apply runs up to 100 operations as one atomic write. The read side still costs one round trip per root. An outline with N top-level roots has no single-call read, because read_subtree takes only a node id; and search hits carry custom properties uncut but not the node's note, so \"read every bug with its note\" degrades into one read_node per hit.\n\nTwo halves, one pull request:\n(a) read_subtree accepts a file as an alternative to an id — the whole outline, every root nested, in one call, with the depth limit still applying, and a mistyped path refused with the closest path that does exist, exactly as read_document already refuses one.\n(b) search_nodes hits carry the note, so a selection with its notes is one call. Whether that is always on or opt-in is the implementer's argument to make: notes can carry long forensic detail, and a query that never reads them should not pay for them.\n\nThe tool descriptions and the hand-written argument types move with the schema.","created":"2026-08-21T13:06:44-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21, orchestrator chat — both halves ratified as ONE PR, dispatched to Opus"}}
{"id":"chat-lifecycle-logs","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a5","title":"PR: the chat logs its lifecycle — sessions, prompts, agent exits — and gets a log-level knob #infra","done":"2026-08-22T08:52:50-04:00","desc":"- Today the journal of a production olai says nothing about chat beyond \"chat agent started\": no conversation opened, no session id, no prompt sent or ended, no agent subprocess spawn/exit, no turn failure. The 2026-08-22 silent-send incident was undiagnosable from the server — six restarts of journal, zero chat lines.\n- **There is no log-level knob at all**: `OLAI_LOG` picks the face (logfmt/pretty) only. The `logDebug` lines that exist — notably the agent's STDERR (agent.ts:826), where opencode writes its errors — cannot be switched on in production.\n\n**Ship:**\n- A level knob (`OLAI_LOG_LEVEL`, default info), documented beside `OLAI_LOG` in docs/running.md; the systemd/HM unit can raise it.\n- INFO lines for the chat's lifecycle, each annotated with agent + session id: agent subprocess spawned (command) / exited (code, signal); conversation opened (new/loaded, which agent); prompt sent; turn ended (stopReason, duration) or failed (the error, verbatim); message queued behind a running turn.\n- The agent's stderr at WARN when a turn fails (and DEBUG otherwise) — opencode dumps its JSON-RPC errors there.\n- Keep the house rule intact: the transcript still surfaces every failure to the person; the journal is for the operator.\n\n**pr** — OLAI_LOG_LEVEL (env wins when set; --log-level works when unset) + HM option; INFO lifecycle lines with agent + session (spawn after handshake, opened, prompt sent as bytes, turn ended/failed, queued, exit); a failed turn's stderr at WARN; opencode do-not-object, folded; CI 9/9","see":["opencode-send-silent"],"created":"2026-08-22T07:42:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T08:52:50-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22, from the #336 silent-send journal","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/1fd22214","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/342"}}
{"id":"bwb-implement","parent":"bun-watcher-bump","ord":"a0","title":"Implementation: pin nixpkgs to the Bun update, check file descriptors and the suites, open the PR #infra","done":"2026-08-24T16:46:33-04:00","desc":"Reported at 16:45 after 33 minutes 14 seconds in terminal 7994f86d: nixpkgs is pinned to the head of nixpkgs pull request #556047, which brings Bun in at version 1.4.0. File descriptor measurements: a clean watch went from 1053 to 14, and a git-shaped corpus from 2058 to 14. All nine kinds of file change still deliver their events, including the two that produced no event at all on Bun 1.3.13 — a file created and then edited inside a directory that appeared after startup, the blind spot that version had. Typecheck clean; unit tests 3593 plus 77 passing with none failing; end-to-end 913 of 914, the one failure being a shared-scratch resynchronisation flake in an After hook, which was recorded and passed 3 of 3 when retried in isolation. No deferred work.\n\nPull request opened at commit adc788ba.","created":"2026-08-24T16:10:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/368","stripped":"17:14 — private master-red fixes removed on the orchestrator's order; diff is pin-only again; wordIn and evidence.ts back to pre-dedup originals; typecheck goes green from master when the repair lands","terminal":"7994f86d"}}
{"id":"bwb-review-pi","parent":"bun-watcher-bump","ord":"a1","title":"Review by the pi agent (session split off the author's) #infra","done":"2026-08-24T17:25:47-04:00","desc":"The pi agent objected, with two blocking findings, reviewing across a moving head commit (adc788ba to a611bce3) at 17:24 over about 35 minutes: https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/368#issuecomment-5401480175\n\n- Blocking finding 1: the nixpkgs-for-Bun pin records a branch that does not exist on the owner it names, so `just update-pins` fails outright — the real upstream head is hesprs/nixpkgs, branch bun-1.4-update.\n- Blocking finding 2: the suite numbers in the pull request description come from an earlier commit; the pushed head's unit test step is red, from a break on master introduced by PR #371 — proven identical under the Bun 1.3.13 binary, so it is not a consequence of the runtime change.\n\nVerified against the description: the pinned revision is exactly refs/pull/556047/head, nothing else moves in sources.json, upstream touches only bun, kilo, cyberstrike and anytype, the file descriptor receipts were reproduced (1.3.13: 1050 and 2055; 1.4.0: one descriptor for the watch), the nine kinds of file change match byte for byte, the changelog scan is clean for the surface olai uses, and the attribution of the load-related flake holds.\n\nRecommendations, both for the orchestrator: refresh the roadmap node at merge, and record the After-hook flake. Minor notes: the bun-types package lags the runtime version; the mutation script exists only in the gitignored .probe/ directory.","after":["bwb-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:10:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T09:18:53-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-pi","terminal":"d40b18e5"}}
{"id":"bwb-close","parent":"bun-watcher-bump","ord":"a2","title":"Apply the review, run CI once, merge (pre-approved by the human) #infra","done":"2026-08-24T18:03:42-04:00","desc":"Closed at 18:05. Both of the pi agent's blocking findings were applied — the pin re-recorded against the real owner, hesprs/nixpkgs branch bun-1.4-update, with `just update-pins` exiting 0 and the revision unchanged at d2f0dc92; and the pull request description re-quoted from the pushed commit — along with both minor notes: bun-types and @types/bun moved to 1.4.0, and the mutation script was published in docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md. On a repaired master the local checks were green at commit bec1f916: typecheck across 14 packages, 3593 plus 77 unit tests with none failing, and end-to-end 914 of 914 — the After-hook flake did not reproduce. CI passed 10 of 10 on the kolu-ci-5 runner. Merged as fb3a0cfc (squash) on the human's pre-approval given at 16:52. The two recommendations were the orchestrator's own: this roadmap node is closed by the merge, and the After-hook flake is already recorded in the Inbox as afterhook-resync-flaky. Working tree removed, branch deleted, terminal 7994f86d retired.","after":["bwb-review-pi"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:10:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00"}
{"id":"wtf-implement","parent":"web-testlib-face","ord":"a0","title":"Implementation: add the ./testlib export and open the PR #infra","done":"2026-08-24T17:15:02-04:00","desc":"Reported at 17:14 from terminal 0956e8cf. The new entry point is a curated `./testlib` export on @olai/web: 32 deep-path import statements across 17 files became one import per file, and support/world.ts's five collapsed into a single line. All three places where the manifest told a falsehood were rewritten — package.json's `//exports` comment, the sentence claiming testids.ts was the only thing imported across a package boundary, and the web README's \"No exports, on purpose\", which now reads \"One subpath, no root: ./testlib\" — and the tests README and both manifests' comments now agree. The guard test moved with the export and grew: the sweep now covers the whole package (the old one missed evidence.ts and other drivers) and imports.test.ts pins the export list to contain no components, by proving it carries no .tsx files. Unit tests: 72 of 72 in the tests package, 1246 of 1246 in web. The whole end-to-end suite through the development binary: 913 of 914, with the one failure classified — the pinned-shelf locator in trash.feature line 53 under four-worker load, which passed 11 of 11 alone and 3 of 3 targeted, and the diff changes no product bytes. Steps failing because of the break on master were marked pre-existing by commit, per instruction, rather than fixed here. No deferred work. An earlier stop-and-ask — this session is what discovered the break on master — was resolved through the repair work session.\n\nPull request opened at commit 3f480f7f.","created":"2026-08-24T16:12:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T09:18:53-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/372","terminal":"0956e8cf"}}
{"id":"wtf-review-grok","parent":"web-testlib-face","ord":"a1","title":"Review by the Grok agent (session split off the author's) #infra","done":"2026-08-24T17:27:19-04:00","desc":"The Grok agent did not object, with no blocking findings, at commit 3f480f7f (17:26, 9 minutes 40 seconds): https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/372#issuecomment-5401571529\n\nTwo things to fix before merging: the no-components assertion only string-matches .tsx on the export file itself, so a re-export of a re-export would be invisible (imports.test.ts line 69); and the rewritten README line 359 still says \"never behaviour\", while the export's fourth group exports `completingIn`, which chat_steps calls as a function. The curation was judged real — a grouped, deliberate export list rather than a barrel file.","after":["wtf-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:12:24-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"fa7b3ae3"}}
{"id":"wtf-close","parent":"web-testlib-face","ord":"a2","title":"Apply the review, run CI once, merge automatically on green #infra","done":"2026-08-24T18:05:56-04:00","desc":"Closed at 18:06. Both of the Grok agent's points landed in commit 1bf0f9f8:\n1. The no-components assertion now walks the export's whole readable closure — every relative specifier, whether an import or a re-export, position-matched, reachable from suite.testlib.ts — and fails, naming the link, on any .tsx it reaches. It was proven by replanting the reviewer's own example: near.ts re-exporting Transcript.tsx made it fail, naming the file. Non-relative specifiers stop the walk, since another package's discipline is its own concern.\n2. \"never behaviour\" was more false than the reviewer found: it is restated in the tests README and package.json as \"no machinery\" — the furthest an import goes is a pure read — with the export file's own header comment as the authority.\n\nChecks after merging master: typecheck clean in all packages, 3671 unit tests passing, end-to-end 914 with 2 failures, both from the documented flake family (the palette_actions capture wait passed 2 of 2 targeted; zoom_and_navigate line 113's scroll restoration was measured as a flake on master, with product bytes verbatim). CI green — the human confirmed, 15 of 15 checks. Merged as 42987d90 (squash) under the pre-authorized gate. Working tree removed, branch deleted, terminal 0956e8cf retired.","after":["wtf-review-grok"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:12:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00"}
{"id":"d3c-implement","parent":"debate3-claim-tests","ord":"a0","title":"Implementation: pin claims (a) and (b) as tests, open the PR #infra","done":"2026-08-24T17:01:36-04:00","desc":"Reported at 17:00 from terminal f08e8207, after stripping out its private fixes for the break on master on the orchestrator's instruction: one commit, 2 files, 88 lines added and 1 removed.\n\nClaim (a), that address recognition has one door, is pinned twice: by a sweep over the source (`parseAddress(` is called only in routes.ts, and a second recognizer makes the test fail with its file named; workspace.ts's splitAddress is covered by a comment saying it splits rather than recognizes), and by a behaviour test over the full mintable vocabulary, bare and named, asserting that addressIn's answer is routeIn's route and that what the door refuses a title refuses too — which pins the promise that a pin and a written link cannot come to two answers.\n\nClaim (b) is pinned by a literal-specifier sweep: every dynamic `import()` in the client takes a literal the bundler can read — the edge the existing chunk sweeps miss.\n\nBoth sweeps were verified by deliberately breaking the code: a probe recognizer made the first fail, naming address/address.ts, and `import(spec)` made the second fail, naming menu/chunk.ts; both were reverted.\n\nOn its own diff: 43 tests passing with none failing across the two files, 90 assertions. Full-suite steps stay red until the repair for master lands — a repository-wide problem, stated in the pull request description. No deferred work.\n\nPull request opened at commit 0ef6f8c9.","created":"2026-08-24T16:12:26-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T09:18:53-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/370","terminal":"f08e8207"}}
{"id":"d3c-review-grok","parent":"debate3-claim-tests","ord":"a1","title":"Review by the Grok agent (session split off the author's) #infra","done":"2026-08-24T17:10:56-04:00","desc":"The Grok agent did not object, with no blocking findings, at commit 0ef6f8c9 (17:10, 7 minutes 16 seconds): https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/370#issuecomment-5401413461\n\nIt reproduced one of the sweep's deliberate breakages itself — a probe recognizer added to address.ts made the test fail, naming the file, and was reverted — and reproduced the file-scoped result of 43 tests, none failing, 90 assertions; it found no leftover repairs for the master break and no junk.\n\nTwo recommendations: the \"full mintable vocabulary\" is a hand-written list (address.test.ts line 46) and should be enumerated from the grammar or it will go stale; and the `import()` assertion only checks that the next character is a quote (claims.test.ts line 441), so `import(\"./Dropdown.tsx\" + \"\")` would pass — tighten the pattern.","after":["d3c-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:12:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"69e0d3e0"}}
{"id":"d3c-close","parent":"debate3-claim-tests","ord":"a2","title":"Apply the review, run CI once, merge automatically on green #infra","done":"2026-08-24T17:36:49-04:00","desc":"Closed at 17:38. Both recommendations were taken:\n1. The hand-written vocabulary became grammar-driven — the ROUTES table moved to routes.testlib.ts as one shared table read by both the round-trip test and the delegation test, and was extended with a block enumerated from @olai/format's FILE_KINDS; hrefOf's percent-encoding was verified, with 43 routes and zero mismatches.\n2. The `import()` assertion now requires one complete quoted string argument before the closing parenthesis. The reviewer's `import(\"./Dropdown.tsx\" + \"\")`, a variable, and a template literal were all re-witnessed failing.\n\nChecks on the merged tree: typecheck silent across 14 packages, 3596 unit tests passing with none failing, 77 browser steps passing. Strict CI at commit b621d1c: 10 checks ok. Merged as de40d859 (squash) under the pre-authorized green-CI gate; working tree removed, branch deleted, terminal f08e8207 retired.","after":["d3c-review-grok"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:12:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00"}
{"id":"chr-implement","parent":"child-receptacle","ord":"a0","title":"Implementation: build @olai/child, list the subprocess owners, open the PR #infra","done":"2026-08-24T16:22:09-04:00","desc":"Reported at 16:20 after 30 minutes 6 seconds in terminal 5976f8ab. The new @olai/child package owns starting a process, a typed execution failure, drained stderr, and killing with a grace period. The pull request carries the map of owners: chat's pipes and its kolu driver, the git runner, format's committing code, the server's serve and edit paths, and web's Tailwind build — each either migrated or already using it; main.ts is out of scope, covered by PR #355's PDEATHSIG sweep; child.testlib uses it too, with waiting for the serving line left as residue. Real deletions: 787 lines added and 270 removed across 25 files, including stoppedWithin and git's own execFile. The ride-along fixes were folded in, including the recorded logLevel wait (minor note 4 from PR #364 — merging this closes the loglevel-test-stoppedwithin node). The sidecar build and the embedder tests were left alone: no consumer, parked with the recall work. Suites: @olai/child 13 passing none failing, targeted 414 passing none failing, the full unit run 3598 with one failure in evidence.ts claimed to pre-exist on master, to be verified at close; the Nix build green; end-to-end 111 scenarios / 1180 steps. No deferred work.\n\nPull request opened at commit c2704bc6.","created":"2026-08-24T16:18:36-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/367","terminal":"5976f8ab"}}
{"id":"chr-review-pi","parent":"child-receptacle","ord":"a1","title":"Review by the pi agent (session split off the author's) #infra","done":"2026-08-24T17:07:24-04:00","desc":"The pi agent did not object but raised one blocking finding, at commit c2704bc6 (17:06, about 40 minutes): https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/367#issuecomment-5401370731\n\nThe blocking finding, probed mechanically with a 100 KB child process and a 64 KB cap: the maxBuffer contract is inverted. The old execFile answered with ok:false and a RangeError once past the cap; the new implementation silently keeps the tail (child.ts lines 164-171, via git.ts line 121), which reaches `dirty`'s porcelain parsing and `show` — quietly wrong answers above 32 MB. Suggested fix: an overflow flag on `take`, with `run` answering ok:false and quoting the tail.\n\nFirst-hand verification trail: master was cross-checked at commit fb0e1b34 and the failures claimed to pre-exist are identical there; the arithmetic of the counts closes exactly (13 tests added in child, 2 removed from pipes); the Nix build is green; end-to-end 111 of 111; three loaded rounds of four-way parallelism passed 12 of 12 with both index.lock assertions passing; and every place claimed to be left alone has had its one-line justification verified.","after":["chr-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:18:41-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T09:20:31-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-pi","terminal":"afc2b8d1"}}
{"id":"chr-close","parent":"child-receptacle","ord":"a2","title":"Apply the review, run CI once, verify the owner map, merge #infra","done":"2026-08-24T18:00:44-04:00","desc":"Closed at 18:00. The pi agent's blocking finding was folded in at 17:15 — an overflow now raises loudly, pinned with the reviewer's own probe shape. After PR #371's repair: master merged, full local checks green (typecheck across 15 members, 3605 unit tests plus 77 browser steps, touched end-to-end 111 scenarios / 1180 steps), strict CI at commit 2d26afd2 with 10 checks ok, and the local run held under the file lock.\n\nThe orchestrator's verification of the owner map against the merged head: @olai/child is the one owner of the primitive — node:child_process spawn appears only in child.ts; agent.ts uses start(); git.ts's execFile is gone; build.ts's Bun.spawn is gone; child.testlib's stoppedWithin is gone; pipes.ts is transport-only, unstartable only as a documentation pointer; chat.ts's spawn() is the conversation-row generator, not a process; main.ts is untouched, its PDEATHSIG remaining PR #355's business.\n\nMerged as 834fbd45 (squash) — working tree removed, branch deleted, terminal 5976f8ab retired.","after":["chr-review-pi"],"created":"2026-08-24T16:18:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00"}
{"id":"brain-vault","parent":"infra-process","ord":"a4","title":"The brain: this vault moves to its own repo — one vault per orchestrator, a folder per project #infra","done":"2026-08-28T11:04:06-04:00","desc":"The design is olai/brainstorming/brain.md, ruled with the human 2026-08-24; the destination became https://github.com/juspay/oss.olai at execution.\n\nCOMPLETE 2026-08-28: the extraction (1,189 commits of real history, reshaped — orchestrator/ and _olai/ at the root, the olai project folder holding roadmap, brainstorming, RCA, lowy-electricity; working material untracked and ignored), the human's push, the removal from the olai repo (PR #414, merged as fd8ad02e), and the production server repointed at a checkout of this repo. The orchestrator now boots from here — the session serving the old vault ended with the repoint.","created":"2026-08-24T18:14:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T11:04:20-04:00"}
{"id":"verdict-shape","parent":"infra-model","ord":"aC","title":"PR: validation's result becomes structured data instead of a flat error log #infra","done":"2026-08-25T20:32:18-04:00","desc":"@olai/format's error value `E` stops being a flat log that every consumer re-partitions, wrongly. The result carries structure:\n- Which files each finding implicates (the `Reach` type in errors.ts is the starting point).\n- `admits(files) → ok | implicated(file, rows)` for the write gate, so the whole-set boolean becomes impossible to express: one broken file can never again freeze writes to healthy files, and a refusal names what is blocking it.\n- A bounded per-file `summary(n)` for any surface to draw, so the banner shows counts rather than 135 rows and the flood stays off the wire.\n- Severity tiers for set-wide rules. The per-line tier already exists — files that fail to parse degrade in place — and set-wide rules get their missing half, which is what makes the cold-boot policy something that can be written down.\n\nConsumers: the ops layer's write gate calls admits; the banner draws summary; boot consults the tier. The store stays generic (store.ts line 8: \"not one olai type in here\"); the result rides the existing errors cell as a shaped `E`.\n\nGuards on top, not instead: the banner clamp, and the errors cell's join pinned for the last-good-with-rows and unreadable cases (face.test.ts lines 213-241 already holds half of it).","see":["broken-file-blocks-healthy-writes","last-good-banner-flood","cold-boot-all-or-nothing"],"created":"2026-08-25T18:58:22-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/vs.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T19:12:00-04:00","from":"the 2026-08-25 lowy-electricity debate (finding 2, ratified) — brainstorm: lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-25.md","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/7b6e6ecf2684788ae28f3bd163522829815c64c8","merged":"2026-08-25T20:31:00-04:00","worktree":".worktrees/verdict-shape"}}
{"id":"verdict-boot-policy","parent":"infra-model","ord":"aD","title":"Which validation failures should refuse to start the app? — the human's call #infra","todo":true,"desc":"The design debate deliberately refused to smuggle this policy into the architecture: validate.ts line 188's blanket rule — any set-wide error refuses the whole set — becomes a severity tier that code can consult, and which classes of failure are fatal at startup is a single ruling for the human to make. The incident that prompted it, the same day: two dangling `see` edges served an entirely empty vault, chat included.\n\nWaits on the verdict-shape work, which is what makes the tier expressible.","after":["verdict-shape"],"created":"2026-08-25T18:58:22-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00"}
{"id":"vintage-reads","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a6","title":"PR: every read of the set carries how old it is and how that was checked #infra","done":"2026-08-25T23:21:46-04:00","desc":"@olai/store's read result gains a **Vintage** — as of when, and how it was verified — and a consumer cannot obtain the set without one; this is enforced by the types, not by discipline.\n\nThe non-negotiable constraint, proposed by the Grok agent and signed by every seat: the vintage's verification path does not share the publishing fiber's permit, so a wedged publish loop yields a visibly stale vintage and never a fresh-looking lie.\n\nWhat this kills: store.ts line 405's settled `null` — a probe that finds an identical stamp publishes nothing, which makes a missed rebase impossible to represent as an error. That is the mechanism behind the 30 minutes of silent staleness on 2026-08-25.\n\nCallers state a freshness class — cheap, straight off the snapshot, for redrawing the UI; verified, for a tool result an agent will act on — and never the means: stamps, re-stats and cadence stay behind the door, and `resync`'s stamp folklore retires there rather than being re-hired one floor up (the opencode agent's closing argument).\n\nGuards: the MCP read joins the vintage, and \"no successful read without a vintage\" is pinned as a type test.","see":["stale-set-reads-clean-writes-refuse"],"created":"2026-08-25T18:58:33-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:22-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/vr.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T22:12:00-04:00","from":"the 2026-08-25 lowy-electricity debate (finding 3, ratified; grok's red line is the shape) — brainstorm: lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-25.md","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/e01a87638cf0d8fc9d2d3971901ef4999f190ded","merged":"2026-08-25T23:29:00-04:00","worktree":".worktrees/vintage-reads"}}
