{"id":"kolu-screen-tail","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"aG","title":"Upstream: let kolu's screen.text ask for the last N lines #nightly #infra","todo":true,"desc":"padi's `screen.text` — padi being kolu's terminal service — takes absolute startLine and endLine, and kaval, the layer above it, clamps only the low side. So \"the last N lines\" cannot be expressed without knowing the buffer's length, and `startLine: N` returns an empty string for any buffer shorter than N. kaval already has the answer: `resolveScreenExtent` is a closed union of full, range, tail and viewport, but only `range` reaches padi's wire.\n\nWho pays today: three consumers take the tail themselves, client-side, over the whole rendered buffer — kolu's own MCP face, `kolu snapshot --tail`, and olai's snapshot pane. Three copies of one operation, and a whole scrollback transferred per read.\n\nThe ask: widen PadiScreenTextInputSchema with an optional `tail` (or with the whole ScreenExtent union, which also gives `viewport`, something a caller cannot compute). Additive and optional. Not urgent, and deliberately not amended into kolu PR #2216: the contract as it stands is honest and olai fixed its own usage; what this buys is wire cost and the removal of the third copy, not correctness.\n\nBatching rule, agreed at the fifth sitting on 2026-08-26: this does not ride along with the dock-row pull request, because two asks in one contract bump costs a version pin. If part 1 of terminal-door-polish — the screenshot pane — re-opens the screen.* procedure, batch this tail request with that payment: one procedure, one kolu pull request, when that wire actually moves.","created":"2026-08-25T23:04:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:48:44-04:00","custom":{"from":"#405's author consuming kolu#2216 (pi's review MUST), 2026-08-25"}}
{"id":"vault-extraction-pr","parent":"brain-vault","ord":"a0","title":"olai draft PR: the vault's directories leave, links point at oss.olai #infra","done":"2026-08-28T11:04:02-04:00","desc":"MERGED as fd8ad02e (2026-08-28), authored by a Claude Opus subagent in an isolated worktree (the human's instruction — no kolu terminal). What it did: deleted the moved vault directories from docs/ (71 tracked files), pointed CLAUDE.md at https://github.com/juspay/oss.olai, rewrote 301 citations across 172 files to /blob/main/ URLs, and re-homed the four real-vault test suites onto a third npins pin (oss-olai) whose store path the dev shell exports as OSS_OLAI_VAULT — the tests throw loudly when it is absent, never skip; floors and queries unchanged. Suites green at merge; no deferrals.","created":"2026-08-28T09:40:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T11:04:05-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/vault-extraction.md","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/414"}}
