{"id":"mcp-node-reads","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"aM","title":"MCP node reads say their parent's id, and read_subtree can skip notes #infra","done":"2026-08-28T12:28:40-04:00","desc":"MERGED as squash b22ab85f (2026-08-28), same-day from the morning's incident: the orchestrator needed one parent id and the only deterministic route was a 90k-character whole-outline read.\n\nWhat shipped: (1) `parent` (the parent node's id, omitted at top-level roots) on every situated answer — read_node, subtree rows, child lists, search hits — derived in one place; (2) `withDesc` on `read_subtree`, default true (byte-identical answers for existing callers), `false` the lean structural read — the incident's exact read drops 94,202 → 25,060 chars. Tool descriptions teach the lean idiom.\n\nThe lane's one CI stumble, settled by measurement: published.equivalence.test.ts timed out on the loaded localhost box (6718ms vs bun's 5s default) while green on the pool; branch vs master on the same box measured 2119ms vs 1992ms mean — not this PR's cost — so the case's budget went to 15s with the numbers in the commit message. Review: pi, APPROVE (verdict on the review step). Evidence frame-verified against this vault itself.","see":["mcp-read-batch"],"created":"2026-08-28T11:23:21-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:07-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/mcp-node-reads.md","dispatched":"2026-08-28T11:21:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/b22ab85f","merged":"2026-08-28T12:29:00-04:00","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/416","terminal":"866e3da4","worktree":".worktrees/mcp-node-reads"}}
