{"id":"sigterm-refuse","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a7","title":"PR: the server refuses unattributed TERMs and names their sender #infra","done":"2026-08-29T12:26:49-04:00","desc":"Solution 1 of the deterministic ban (brainstorming/deterministic-ban.md), dispatched on the human's word after the 2026-08-29 double-kill incident (RCA beside this roadmap): sigaction+SA_SIGINFO via a native shim — TERM honored only from kernel/self/the supervising parent; every other sender logged with pid/uid/cmdline and refused, async-signal-safely. SIGKILL stays uncatchable by design; auditd (solution 3) is the human's repo. Shipped as its own package (packages/sigterm) per the human's review-time ruling; darwin returns early, the .c never compiles there.\n\nCI EXCEPTION (the human, 2026-08-29 ~11:00): green on BOTH platforms — the .c module.\n\n**MERGE AUTHORIZATION STANDING** (the human, 2026-08-29 12:20, \"sigterm PR approved\"): the orchestrator merges without a further ask once the watcher's both-platform run posts green at the residue head 5373e599 and the body's transcripts check out.","created":"2026-08-29T09:50:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T12:32:21-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","approved":"2026-08-29T12:20:00-04:00","brief":"briefs/sigterm-refuse.md","dispatched":"2026-08-29T09:52:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/426","terminal":"258146eb","tier":"ordinary","timings":"implement 47m14s (pi) · refactor 12m41s (pi) · review(∥) 18m12s (grok+opus) · address 50m26s (pi) · ci(both) 26m7s (claude-ci) · close 4s (orch) — TOTAL 2h34m44s (09:52→12:26)","worktree":".worktrees/sigterm-refuse"}}
