{"id":"lane-str-review-a","parent":"sigterm-refuse","ord":"a2","title":"review: grok #infra","done":"2026-08-29T11:10:06-04:00","after":["lane-str-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-29T09:50:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T11:10:06-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-grok","terminal":"3fa4e9b3","verdict":"APPROVE, no MUST (probe-backed: glibc sigaction layout confirmed; ppid live on bun 1.4.0). SHOULDs: honor path ignores sigaction-restore failure (a broken restore re-catches the re-raise and the stop waits for SIGKILL); dropped++ non-atomic in the C; drain swallows non-EAGAIN read errors + POSIX coalescing means the docs' every-sender-named overclaims. NITs: two false comments about the restored disposition; the reparenting test stubs the parent. Comment 5463154784."}}
{"id":"lane-str-review-b","parent":"sigterm-refuse","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus #infra","done":"2026-08-29T11:10:07-04:00","after":["lane-str-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-29T09:50:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T11:10:07-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","terminal":"6e1e9251","verdict":"REQUEST CHANGES. MUST: the PDEATHSIG premise is wrong on Linux — a parent-death TERM arrives from the dying parent's pid with SI_USER, not si_pid 0, so judge() refuses it and the server silently stops dying with its parent (an existing tested feature disarmed; the error is repeated in the C, TS, unit test, PR body, docs). Also: verified() discards the batch after the self-test record; drain treats every read error as EAGAIN (unstoppable-and-silent failure mode); \"userspace cannot forge si_pid 0\" overclaims (rt_sigqueueinfo validates only si_code). Comment 5463121936."}}
