{"id":"agent-roster-plugins","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a8","title":"PR: the agent roster becomes plugins #infra","todo":true,"desc":"DEEPENED by the eighth sitting's ratified conclusion (projects/olai/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-31.md, the human 2026-09-01) — the design is now binding for this lane: one plugin PER AGENT, never one roster plugin; @olai/acp stays a general package; each agent's adapter pins and patches ride its own plugin (plugin-claude inherits the 0.66.0-patch debt); a NEW optional `agent` hook on the server half (never overloading probe()); AGENTS in @olai/surface becomes data; models.ts's Claude bets, per-agent marks, and NoAgent.tsx's install sentences travel; acp-system-prompt's TEXT stays one core module while the CHANNEL is each agent plugin's.","created":"2026-08-31T09:32:18-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T14:53:30-04:00"}
{"id":"lowy-sitting-8","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a9","title":"The eighth sitting: what else becomes a plugin #infra","done":"2026-09-01T14:53:30-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T10:25:26-04:00","worked":102484,"desc":"RATIFIED (the human, 2026-09-01): the conclusion is filed at projects/olai/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-31.md — no plugin-orchestrator (the driver is a wire client, the page is a core reading, the practice stays vault data); one-plugin-per-agent deepens the roster lane; the ledgered conditions and standing negatives roll forward. One amendment at ratification: the recall sequencing choice was superseded — recall is DROPPED entirely (semantic-recall-parked carries the ruling).","created":"2026-08-31T10:25:26-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T14:53:30-04:00","custom":{"brief":"debates/lowy-electricity-2026-08-31/charter.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T10:25:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-08-31 ~10:25"}}
{"id":"fdo-residuals","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"aA","title":"PR: close two test holes noted in #449 #infra","done":"2026-08-31T15:58:09-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T15:27:17-04:00","worked":1852,"desc":"Two tiny test-hygiene holes the #449 re-verdict named at file:line and deliberately left unchased — neither can bite today, both are the kind that bites later:\n\n1. **`packages/ops/src/plans.golden.test.ts:151` — a removal prunes two of the three corpora.** When the golden harness replays a file removal it prunes the `texts` and `bodies` corpora but not `bare`, the third list. Harmless right now only by accident: the sole bare entry is `notes/page.html`, which the delete verb refuses by kind anyway. The same hole, one list over from the one it does prune — the fix is one more prune line plus whatever pin keeps the three lists from drifting apart again.\n\n2. **The new outline-delete e2e scenario marks the page and never checks the mark.** The scenario (in the delete family, document_editing.feature) sets a page-mark whose assertion never runs because the following step (\"I open the outline\") re-navigates through `/`. Harmless and consistent with the scenario beside it — but an assertion that never runs is a test that claims more than it checks: either check the mark before the navigation or drop the mark.\n\nMechanical tier: ~twenty lines across two test files, zero product code. Proposed: grok authors, pi reviews, auto-merge — and as a third live lane it thickens the doorbell probe's traffic. AWAITING THE HUMAN'S DISPATCH WORD.","created":"2026-08-31T15:25:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:42:02-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/fdo-residuals.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T15:30:00-04:00","from":"opus's #449 re-verdict (comment 5482584491), noted non-blocking; captured on the human's ask 2026-08-31 ~15:27","kolu-terminal":"4e74f19d","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/ac9167a7","merged":"2026-08-31","o