{"id":"appliance-fold","parent":"infra-build","ord":"aA","title":"PR: kolu's packages fold into its plugin #nightly #infra","done":"2026-08-31T23:50:36-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T20:37:50-04:00","worked":11566,"desc":"Two structural changes in one PR, both the human's word (2026-08-31), to run OVERNIGHT.\n\n**1. The appliance fold.** `kolu-ui` and `kolu-client` stop being their own packages and become module directories inside the kolu plugin — one identity per appliance instead of three. The seventh lowy-electricity sitting already ratified this for `kolu-ui` (its record: \"plugin-kolu absorbs the wire slice and kolu-ui\"); the human extends it to `kolu-client`.\n\n**2. The rename.** The tenants move to `packages/plugins/olai-plugin-kolu` and `packages/plugins/olai-plugin-odu` — the prefix says what the thing is, the way every ecosystem names its plugins.\n\n**The two questions the design round must rule, both named before dispatch:**\n\n- **The dial's wall.** `kolu-client` is the dial — the padi client, detect, `koluHalf`. Today it imports no olai package and the COMPILER proves that; a fence that walks doors cannot tell a dial module from a plugin module once they share a package. So folding it in trades a compiler-enforced boundary for a convention. Either the dial keeps its own package (two per appliance, which the sitting called the honest end state) or it folds and the fence grows a FILE-LEVEL claim for dial modules. Whichever is chosen, the enforcement must be as strong afterwards as it is today — that is the bar, not the layout.\n- **Where the interface lives.** `packages/plugins` is today the interface package `@olai/plugins` — the one package a plugin may not import. Putting tenants inside its directory makes the fence's own graph walk and the workspace globs read as contradictions. The interface should move out (`packages/plugin-api/`, or a nested `packages/plugins/interface/`) so `packages/plugins/` is purely the tenant container.\n\n**The bar:** every existing behavior identical, the fence and mechanics lints as strong as before (prove it — a mutation that should fail must still fail), the nix build, the docs symlinks and the docs assembly all following the move. Wide blast radius and distant invariants, so claude-opus authors; grok and pi review.","created":"2026-08-31T16:37:22-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T23:50:36-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/appliance-fold.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T20:38:00-04:00","from":"the human 2026-08-31 ~16:36; the fold half was ratified by the seventh lowy sitting (debate-2026-08-30)","kolu-terminal":"855de957","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/02190f27","merged":"2026-09-01","odu-worktree":".worktrees/appliance-fold","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/453","tier":"design-heavy","timings":"implement 1h11m (opus) · refactor 1h19m · reviews 12m27s/12m21s parallel (grok/pi, 0 MUST 8 SHOULD 3 NIT) · merge-master skipped · address 16m06s · ci 12m23s (claude-ci, 11/11 first attempt) · close <1m — TOTAL 3h12m (20:38→23:50)"}}
