{"id":"lane-appliance-fold-ci","parent":"appliance-fold","ord":"a6","title":"CI green at head #infra","done":"2026-08-31T23:49:38-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T23:37:15-04:00","worked":743,"desc":"claude-ci spawns as a split at close and stays warm for the whole lifecycle. This node carries odu-worktree + pr-url when it goes doing, so the live chip draws here. The verdict is the orchestrator's read of gh, never an agent's claim.","after":["lane-appliance-fold-merge-master","lane-appliance-fold-address"],"created":"2026-08-31T20:37:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T23:49:38-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"d82d7b9f","odu-worktree":".worktrees/appliance-fold","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/453"}}
{"id":"lane-appliance-fold-evidence","parent":"appliance-fold","ord":"a7","title":"evidence verified #infra","done":"2026-08-31T23:49:38-04:00","desc":"VERIFIED, and not by a screenshot — this lane changes no visual face, so its evidence is the proof artefacts the bar actually named, and they are stronger than a photograph because two independent readers attacked them.\n\n- **The fence proof, proven both ways at head:** `prove-fence.sh` reports 15 of 15 with every red matching the claim its mutation names, AND a mutation deliberately pointed at a claim it does not trip reports 0 of 1 and exits 1. The harness that could not fail now can, which was the finding the refactor round made against its own earlier number.\n- **Independently checked by both reviewers**, each spending its one allowed probe on it: grok proved out-of-tree that under the pinned bun a module-load death prints no `(fail)` line, so resolution deaths and OOMs cannot score as catches; pi proved the selector guard fires before the baseline without invoking bun at all.\n- **Behaviour identical, measured:** the browser bundle is byte-identical in 8 of 9 assets including the stylesheet; the ninth differs in two places out of 926 KB after normalising identifiers — the chunk's own hashed filename, and one object literal becoming a spread, which is the fold itself.\n- **The machine agreed:** 11 of 11 CI nodes green at 8c700c8, first attempt, no flake.","after":["lane-appliance-fold-ci"],"created":"2026-08-31T20:37:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T23:49:38-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-appliance-fold-deferrals","parent":"appliance-fold","ord":"a8","title":"deferrals ruled #human #infra","done":"2026-08-31T23:49:38-04:00","desc":"GATE CLEAR. The `## Deferrals` section opens with the exact sentence the gate requires — \"No deferrals — nothing this PR owed is unfinished\" — and then lists three DECLINES with their reasons: a leaf contract package, TypeScript composite project references, and a registry-fence claim for the appliance/browser filing line (declined there and held instead in the tenant's own test).\n\nBoth reviewers were asked to judge whether those were deferrals wearing another name, and both independently said they were not: nothing in this lane's bar needed any of them. Two are now board items of their own (`plugin-leaf-contract`, `ts-project-references`), filed by the orchestrator because authors do not write board files — which is what both reviewers asked for, so the declines live somewhere other than a commit message.","after":["lane-appliance-fold-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-31T20:37:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T23:49:38-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-appliance-fold-merge","parent":"appliance-fold","ord":"a9","title":"merge #infra","done":"2026-08-31T23:50:04-04:00","desc":"Auto-merge is the default and no ruling marks this lane otherwise: reviews folded plus CI green at head is the authorization. Read the author's final message first.","after":["lane-appliance-fold-deferrals"],"created":"2026-08-31T20:37:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T23:50:04-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-appliance-fold-retire","parent":"appliance-fold","ord":"aA","title":"retire terminals #infra","done":"2026-08-31T23:50:04-04:00","desc":"Kill every terminal the lane spawned, author included, only after the merge is confirmed. Worktree removal is a separate act afterwards.","after":["lane-appliance-fold-merge"],"created":"2026-08-31T20:37:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T23:50:04-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-appliance-fold-timings","parent":"appliance-fold","ord":"aB","title":"timings posted #infra","done":"2026-08-31T23:50:36-04:00","desc":"The orchestrator's own closing act: the step table as one PR comment, plus odu's per-recipe breakdown, and the summary line onto the lane as a timings prop.","after":["lane-appliance-fold-retire"],"created":"2026-08-31T20:37:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T23:50:36-04:00"}
{"id":"plugin-leaf-contract","parent":"infra-build","ord":"aB","title":"A leaf package for the plugin contract type #infra","todo":true,"desc":"A plugin cannot import the type that imports it — the contract type lives in the same package as the registry that consumes it, so the dependency runs the wrong way for a tenant that wants to name its own shape. The fold's author named a leaf contract package as the answer, argued it was not owed by that lane's bar, and did not build it.\n\nNot a deferral of #453: nothing in that lane's bar needed it. Filed here because the repo's rule is that work lives on the board, and a decline recorded only in a commit message is where future work goes to be forgotten (grok and pi, independently, on #453).","see":["appliance-fold"],"created":"2026-08-31T23:21:26-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai#453's refactor round named it and declined to build it; both reviewers asked for it to be filed rather than left in a commit message"}}
{"id":"ts-project-references","parent":"infra-build","ord":"aC","title":"TypeScript composite project references #infra","todo":true,"desc":"Composite project references would make the workspace's build graph a fact the compiler holds rather than one the test corpus re-derives. The fold's author considered it and recorded an honest limit: it **would not subsume claims 4 and 5** of the fence, so it is an addition rather than a replacement.\n\nNot a deferral of #453 — that lane's bar never needed it. Filed here on both reviewers' request so the decline is a board item rather than a line in a commit message.","see":["appliance-fold"],"created":"2026-08-31T23:21:26-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai#453's refactor round named it and declined to build it; both reviewers asked for it to be filed rather than left in a commit message"}}
{"id":"logging-audit","parent":"infra-server","ord":"aA","title":"Audit logging across the whole app — observability done right #needs-brainstorm #human #infra","todo":true,"desc":"The human's suspicion, 2026-09-01, proven the same evening: our logging is dogshit and needs a perfect job across ALL aspects of the app.\n\n**The proof (provenance):** a P1 doorbell bug — a claimed lane silently dropped from the watcher's ringing set — was undiagnosable from logs. Across 15,611 server log lines only two watcher-related messages existed (\"kolu is on this session\", \"stale tab rejected\"); nothing logged the watcher's derived set, its wake/digest/silence classification, deliveries, nag fires, or the heartbeat's membership. The orchestrator had to reconstruct the whole failure from the chat transcript and `kolu ls`. The earlier `logging` node (Proper logging #techdebt) is marked DONE, yet this is what \"done\" bought — so the audit re-opens the whole question rather than trusting that mark.\n\n**FIRST CONCRETE INPUT (2026-09-01 19:45, verified against the deployed serve):** #462 shipped the watcher tracing that would have made that P1 diagnosable — and it is on the DEBUG channel, so it is silent in a normally-running serve. `OLAI_LOG_LEVEL=debug` turns it on, ALL-OR-NOTHING across every subsystem (packages/server/src/main.ts:133-137). So the logging built to diagnose a supervision failure is invisible exactly when the failure happens, unless debug was already on — and turning it on costs every other subsystem's debug output. That is this audit's central question in one live case: **per-subsystem toggles** (doorbell tracing up without everything else up), and **which lines earn INFO** because their absence is itself the fact a reader needs.\n\n**Scope: every subsystem.** A thorough pass over what each part of the app logs and whether a fault in it is diagnosable from logs alone: the serve/lifecycle, the publish/subscribe loop, the ops layer (writes/commits), the ACP chat bridge, the kolu + odu plugins, CI/odu integration, the wake/doorbell path, error paths and refusals. For each: is there a log line at every decision and failure point, at the right level, with enough structured fields to answer \"why did X happen (or not)\" without a live repro? What is the level discipline (INFO/DEBUG/WARN/ERROR), the field conventions, log volume vs signal, and how a person turns up detail for ONE subsystem?\n\n**Needs a brainstorm + the human's word** before any lane: this is a cross-cutting quality bar, likely several PRs, and the standard (structured logging shape, levels, per-subsystem toggles) is a decision to rule, not for an agent to invent. Brainstorm doc to be written; then phased lanes.","created":"2026-09-01T18:13:12-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T19:46:19-04:00"}
{"id":"flake-shakeout","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"aB","title":"PR: CI re-runs shake out the flakes #infra","done":"2026-09-01T21:40:43-04:00","started":"2026-09-01T21:05:48-04:00","worked":2095,"desc":"The human's overnight order (2026-09-01, going to bed): grok re-runs full CI several times IN SEQUENCE on the kolu-ci pool, fixes every flake surfaced at its cause, one PR carries all fixes, auto-merge on the final green. Loop closes on two consecutive clean runs (≥4 total). Folds in the held deliveries flake (the ledger's flake-deliveries entry — its 09:52 hold is superseded by this order). Ruled: NO REVIEWER — CI is the gate; the flake-class auto-merge grant applies.","created":"2026-09-01T21:05:40-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T21:40:43-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/flake-shakeout.md","dispatched":"2026-09-01T21:15:00-04:00","kolu-terminal":"a74ee546","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/fa0f9ea7","odu-worktree":".worktrees/flake-shakeout","tier":"mechanical","timings":"runs+fix 32m19s (grok, 4 runs, runs 3-4 consecutive green) · merge <1m · TOTAL ~35m (01:15→01:50 UTC)"}}
