{"id":"lane-aap-review-c","parent":"agents-as-plugins","ord":"a3V","title":"review: the Cordis plan's author #infra","done":"2026-09-03T12:10:14-04:00","desc":"**TL;DR.** A second review posted 11:32 ET, \"Review: phase 5 against the brief, by reading\" — by the author of the Cordis plan itself (it says so in its own words: it wrote the phase-5 bullets, calls the keyed session-start door \"simpler than what I wrote\", and ends by pointing at phase 6). NOT DISPATCHED BY THE ORCHESTRATOR; recorded here because the author acted on it and the board must carry what shaped the head. Verdict: **mergeable**, the brief met and two of its lines improved on.\n\n**The three SHOULDs, all taken in a04f5e7e.** (1) `running` on the roster cell was `contributing()`, a union over the five registries, and the tab fetches a row's browser chunk only when `running` is true — so a plugin whose server half registers nothing would be `off` while its fiber is ACTIVE, which phase 9's browser-only dressing plugin would have hit. The fiber's state is the truth and reportBundle already computes it. (2) nix/acp-agent.nix spelled two engines and their patch files a second time; glob the plugin's own directory instead. (3) The engine roster is probed once at boot, before the store opens, which is the second boot-time snapshot after the kind vocabulary — say so where the roster is computed, in propKinds.ts's words, so the loader-surface lane finds both.\n\n**The three NITs:** PromptChannel's one-arm union is the right shape and stays; Claude's install sentence should name the cause; the glossary's engine-rows entry still calls the picker row a slot face.","created":"2026-09-03T12:10:14-04:00"}
{"id":"sidebar-agent-press-scenario","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"aC","title":"PR: the sidebar agent press gets the scenario its step never had #infra","done":"2026-09-03T12:57:26-04:00","started":"2026-09-03T12:16:04-04:00","worked":2482,"desc":"olai issue #487, dispatched by the human 2026-09-03 ~12:18 ET to opencode, NO REVIEW and NO REFACTOR, auto-merge.\n\n`packages/tests/step_definitions/node_agents_steps.ts` defines \"I press the agent {string}\" and no feature calls it. The sibling gesture, the door press, has one scenario. The two are not the same press: `agents/focus.ts` gives the sidebar press BOTH halves — navigate to the node's row, and switch the panel to that agent's conversation — while the door press only switches the panel. So the untested failure is HALF of it working: a press that navigates and leaves the panel alone looks, to a person, exactly like a press that worked, because the page moved.\n\nIt surfaced during a triage, not from the suite: a deployed-build report of \"the sidebar agent navigates but the panel does not change\" turned out to be a stale browser client against a fresh server, not a defect. The gesture is not known-broken; it is uncovered.\n\nThe wrinkle the issue asks to solve properly rather than work around: `@corpus:lanes` holds ONE outline, so the row's route resolves to the page already open and the navigation assertion is vacuous there. Either that corpus gains a second outline or the scenario starts from a corpus that has one.\n\nAlso in the issue, as a second assertion: `open()` returns early and silently when `agent.session === null`. That is the documented intent for an unbound row (\"where the row can only do half of what it means, it does that half\") and it is the shape a real regression would hide in.","created":"2026-09-03T12:16:04-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T12:57:26-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","brief":"briefs/sidebar-agent-press.md","dispatched":"2026-09-03T12:20:00-04:00","issue":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/issues/487","kolu-terminal":"5e8bf89b","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/79b611b3","odu-worktree":".worktrees/sidebar-agent-press","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/488","tier":"ordinary"}}
