{"id":"chat-is-a-plugin","parent":"infra-build","ord":"aK","title":"PR: chat is a plugin, and node agents are scopes inside it #infra","doing":true,"started":"2026-09-03T12:19:24-04:00","desc":"**THE HUMAN OWNS THIS LANE PERMANENTLY, 2026-09-03 ~17:05 ET: \"Drop this, I'm taking over permanently\"** (after taking the terminal over at ~15:30). It is off the day board — the mirror is removed, the `kolu-terminal` and `agent` props are cleared — so no doorbell rings about it and the orchestrator does not supervise, dispatch, review, run CI, merge, restart or report on it. The steps below are left exactly as they stood and are not the orchestrator's to move. The item stays on the roadmap because phase 6 is still phase 6 of the Cordis plan; say the word if it should be trashed instead.\n\nWHERE IT STOOD AT HANDOVER. One commit on branch `chat-is-a-plugin`, UNPUSHED, `ed5b70bc` \"The mechanisms chat needs before it can be a plugin, each green alone\" — groundwork, not the phase 6 PR. About four hours and 5.2M subagent tokens spent on understanding and design before a line was written, hitting the account's daily limit. Two questions were left unanswered: whether to push it, and where the design record goes — fourteen reader reports and five settled rulings in a scratch directory under `/tmp`, which does not survive a reboot.\n\nTWO FINDINGS FROM THAT WORK, worth keeping whatever happens to the branch. (1) THE MCP RENAME HAS NO BLAST RADIUS: chat is on no MCP face at all — the map is five core resources and all 36 tools are `@olai/ops`', nothing on this machine names a chat tool, and `ci-watcher-mcp.json` configures odu only. The plan's \"done means\" clause about announcing the rename in `docs/mcp.md` and the CHANGELOG cannot be met as written: neither file has ever existed. (2) PROCESS-PER-SESSION IS FORCED, NOT CHOSEN: pi-acp calls `closeAllExcept` inside `session/new`, so one process serving many node agents would silently kill agent A's session when B opens; offsetting it, `session/resume` exists in SDK 1.3, so a reaped session respawns without replay.\n\nThe author also reported a mistake against itself: it ran a ten-minute gate it had already delegated, concurrently with fourteen agents, and reported the contended timing as a fact about the branch.\n\nDISPATCH RECORD (superseded). Dispatched by the human 2026-09-03 ~12:32 ET to Claude with ultracode workflows as the method, manual merge, after phase 5 (#486) merged as ff2bd29d. The brief the orchestrator wrote for it was deleted on the human's word ~15:10 ET, along with the practice of the orchestrator authoring instructions at all; it carried an invented sentence (\"token cost is not the constraint here\") that the human never said, and this lane is the evidence for the rule that replaced it.\n\nPhase 6 of `brainstorming/cordis-for-olai.md` §6 is the specification, unchanged: chat stops being core and becomes a plugin row with both halves, and a node agent becomes a Scope opened by that plugin with its sessions as fibers under it. The human's rulings the plan already carries (2026-09-03, through the question tool): a sibling with the MCP tools renamed; chat provides the doors it owns; `agent-session` becomes chat's own prefixed word; node-agent concurrency folds into this lane.","see":["agents-as-plugins","cordis-server","plugin-directories"],"created":"2026-09-03T12:19:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T17:03:55-04:00","custom":{"brief":"briefs/chat-is-a-plugin.md","dispatched":"2026-09-03T12:34:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","odu-worktree":".worktrees/chat-is-a-plugin","tier":"design-heavy"}}
