{"id":"slice4-path-order-landmine","parent":"infra-model","ord":"aF","title":"The delta-frame work must settle on one file-path sort order #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","desc":"**Recorded by the slice-3 author (PR #211):** the patcher places an arriving file by assemble's plain string path compare, while the web client's `sortByPath` sorts segment by segment.\n- The two already disagree today — not new unsoundness.\n- But slice 4 (the browser folding delta frames through the same patcher) has to pick one ordering, or the patched browser view will disagree with the assembled one.\n- Filed on the human's overnight draft ruling (\"file roadmap entries for those three\").\n\n**retired** — verification vs master 44bc6873 — slice 4 landed a third exit: one comparator byPath in @olai/format (paths.ts:42) spent by assemble (set.ts:160), the patcher (patch.ts:291) and the client (web paths.ts:47); orderings pinned by set.test.ts:187,193; and the browser no longer folds through the patcher at all. Nothing left to decide.","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:14-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:08-04:00","custom":{"from":"211","retired":"2026-08-20"}}
{"id":"html-unreadable-refused-state","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aF","title":"An unreadable page says so on the page #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T12:00:00-04:00","desc":"#204's deferral 1.\n- Under load-on-read, an unreadable .html (permissions, vanished mid-read) reports only to the server log — the reader sees the page with no body.\n- Telling them needs a `\"refused\"` state on DocumentEntry (a wire change with its own argument) and a face for it.\n- Still quieter than what it replaced, which failed the whole probe and bannered the whole directory.\n\n**pr** — DocumentEntry gains refused (optional, default false; unreadable-file code only — a frontmatter typo keeps master's blank body + ⚠); bodies.ts and media.ts one story; faces on the page and the DocRef line","created":"2026-08-16T12:49:32-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"204","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/f5aa92e4","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/315"}}
{"id":"patch-refile-fifth-spelling","parent":"infra-model","ord":"aG","title":"The patcher repeats the same reverse-index rebuild five times #techdebt #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T07:41:56-04:00","desc":"Counted during PR #237 by the reuse pass. A reverse index maps a value back to the nodes that hold it; patch.ts maintains five of them and writes the same update by hand each time.\n\n- **The repeated pattern:** containment, namings, mentions, orderings and blockage each walk the same five steps:\n  - Copy the map as it was before the edit.\n  - Build the arriving entries.\n  - Gather the keys the edit could have moved, from both the arriving and the outgoing entries.\n  - For each key, take the surviving entries (filtered by which FILE was touched, not by which record) plus the arriving ones, in a promised order.\n  - Drop the key entirely if it ends up empty, rather than storing an empty list.\n- **PR #237** added the third of these copies, and designed the shared version rather than just skipping past it.\n- A generic `refiled<T>` helper would need the entry's `Located` wrapper projected back out, because the indexes hold differently shaped entries, and it would have to return three things: the rewritten map, the keys that VANISHED, and whether the first namer MOVED.\n- Only `namings` needs the last two, because only `namedBy` promises an order for its keys — two concerns behind one contract, with callers paying for neither unless they ask.\n- **Rule invoked:** the repo's existing author rule — a shared fixture is the right move at four occurrences, not three — means the SIXTH index is what should force the extraction.\n- **Why this node exists:** so that the sixth index triggers the shared version instead of becoming the sixth silent copy.\n- **Status:** the invariants are re-argued for each index today, and `patch.test.ts`'s oracle test is the only thing keeping the copies in step.\n\n**PR:** `refiled<T>` now covers the four genuine copies; orderings and blockage were proven not to be the same shape, with line-by-line evidence in the PR and the review.","created":"2026-08-18T06:05:00-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:08-04:00","custom":{"from":"237","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/4318cbe8","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/307"}}
{"id":"follow-one-unit","parent":"feat-nav","ord":"aI","title":"Fold Link and Tree.tsx into useFollow #techdebt #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #284's merge from its Deferrals (the dag gate: a thing left \"for the human\" becomes a roadmap node).\n- #284 gave router.tsx a `useFollow` — the one tail (`followedSplit` → `openRight`, else `followed` → `go`) — called by PageView's delegated listener and the chat transcript's. Its altitude pass argued that `Link` and `Tree.tsx:396` carry the same two halves (route-off-the-event + open-it) and could be rewired onto it, deleting two exported functions and making the \"one spelling\" claim structural rather than documentary.\n- Not taken there because it is `Link` — every navigation in the app — changed for zero behaviour on a bug-fix PR whose node said do not widen scope. What WAS taken: the two now spell the force bit identically and the Link docstring no longer overclaims.\n- A behaviour-preserving refactor with the whole navigation e2e surface as its net; worth its own small PR when someone is next in router.tsx.\n\n**retired** — verification vs master 44bc6873, the human's ruling — the Tree.tsx half was never true (Tree.tsx:408 is a decline-guard, not a navigation; unchanged since #246), and #284's own comment at router.tsx:345-351 argues Link's exclusion is deliberate (route already in hand; reading it back off the href is a round trip through a string). The promised delete-two-exports payoff is impossible; closed rather than shrunk.","created":"2026-08-20T11:29:01-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #284 deferral","retired":"2026-08-20"}}
{"id":"names-table-once","parent":"feat-nav","ord":"aJ","title":"The names table is built twice per navigation #techdebt #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T09:17:26-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at PR #287's merge, from its \"seen, not touched\" list (raised by the efficiency pass).\n- After #287, the names table lives in `names.ts` and is compared by value, but `App.tsx` (for the app chrome) and each pane (for its own rows) each build one over the focused pane's reading — the same scan done twice per frame.\n- The fix is a field on `createReading` plus a change to the readings register, so the table is derived once beside the reading and read by both. That is not the shape of #287, which was a PR about giving lists their keys.\n- It would be retired or shrunk by the upstream kolu item (`reactivity-kolu-upstream`) if keyed reconciliation lands first, since it is the per-frame re-derivation that makes the double scan cost anything.\n\n**PR:** `createReading` derives the lookup once; the pane leaves and the palette share it; App.tsx's second site was deleted; a claims sweep and a run-count probe fence it in.\n\n**Verified against master commit 44bc6873:** the per-frame half is already fixed by PR #299 (names.ts lines 39-46, measured in names.browsertest.ts lines 167-186: repeated frames and row moves no longer reach the copying code). What survives: both builds still re-run on a navigation or a real rename (names.browsertest.ts lines 190-197), and a duplicate Map is held beside the pane's. Re-scoped to a small tidying fix: derive it once beside the reading (PageView.tsx lines 74 and 77, the register at reading.tsx lines 294-308, and App.tsx line 248).","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:01-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/88470106","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/314","verified":"2026-08-20"}}
{"id":"one-alert-row","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"aA","title":"One markup for the refusal alert row #techdebt #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T07:41:57-04:00","desc":"The palette and the header box hand-roll the `role=\"alert\"` row the filter bar gets from `SaidLine` — one list, one sentence, three markups.\n\nFiled 2026-08-20 at #287's merge from its \"Seen, not touched\".\n- #287's `refusals.ts` unified the refusal SENTENCE across the filter bar, the palette and the header search box, and keyed their lines so a refusal is no longer re-announced per keystroke.\n- What is still three-fold is the MARKUP: the filter bar draws its row through `SaidLine`, the palette and the header box hand-roll theirs. Unifying it is a change to what three surfaces draw — its own small PR, with the live-region behaviour (one announcement per new refusal) pinned.\n\n**pr** — five hand-rolled role=alert rows ride SaidLine; refusals.tsx hoisted to client top","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:05-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:09-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/bb10212f","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/310"}}
{"id":"shortlist-row-freshness","parent":"search","ord":"aL","title":"Shortlist rows carry their own freshness #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T09:25:21-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 from PR #294's deferrals (ruled a strong reason to defer: it is a design change to surfaces that none of that PR's five items name). CORRECTED after grok's third review note — the first filing named the places the wrong way round.\n- PR #294 blocked a stale Enter at the two places the audit named: `Shortlist.tsx` and `completing.tsx`. Still unguarded, and absorbed into this node: the composer, the palette and the header search box, which all take a result over the same primitive; plus Hypertext's own re-scroll on rewrite (PR #294's \"seen, not touched\").\n- The deeper shape: either rows carry their own freshness through `search/Result.tsx` — which all four shortlist entry points already draw — or `createSettled` gains a way of taking a result that cannot fire once the question has moved on. Either one fixes the whole class at once instead of guarding one entry point at a time.\n- The decision it would absorb: a stale Enter is consumed and spends nothing, silently (dimming was rejected as flicker in a campaign about flicker); a pointer press is never blocked.\n\n**PR:** the three taking entry points plus the pointer ruling are pinned by tests, and the Hypertext re-scroll-on-rewrite half is closed by PR #305's landing guard — both halves tracked, nothing quietly dropped (grok's second finding is answered on the PR).","created":"2026-08-20T15:17:36-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:55:59-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #294 deferral","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/e7a5d790","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/312"}}
{"id":"router-owns-spent-landing","parent":"feat-nav","ord":"aK","title":"The router should mark a scroll-to target as used up, where it is created #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T07:41:56-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 from PR #294's deferrals (ruled a strong reason to defer: a design change, not a line — Hypertext still reads the target slug in order to BUILD the frame's URL, so it cannot simply be cleared).\n- A \"landing\" is where a navigation says the page should scroll to. The rule that a landing is acted on only once currently lives in the component that acts on it; router.tsx states the contract but enforces nothing. A `router.landed(…)` call marking a landing as used — still readable, but no longer something to act on — would put the rule where the value is created, and would give the preview pane (PR #286's `useLanding`) the same guard.\n\n**PR:** `Landing` gained a `spent` field with `router.landed` as its only writer; the two Back paths folded into one; three follow-up questions filed as landing-open-questions.","created":"2026-08-20T15:17:40-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #294 deferral","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/f4a8b7ae","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/305"}}
{"id":"filter-highlight-cross-piece","parent":"search","ord":"aJ","title":"A phrase across rendered markdown lights neither piece #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T12:00:00-04:00","desc":"The surviving half of #240's filter-highlight deferral, closed.\n\n- **#254** (a848677d): a needle inside a code span or link lights; the tag SPLIT stays off under NO_TAGS_IN.\n- **This PR:** a phrase spanning two rendered pieces lights both. One `litBy` over the concatenated visible text of the title's HAST nodes; each node is a window onto that search (the `titleParts`/`runsIn` contract, one level up). Matching still folds the raw source (`foldOf`). Palette and header node-hits run the same `renderTitle` (`links: false`). Completions/Shortlist stay text.\n- **Named leftover, not a child:** a fenced block forced inline in a title — a phrase that crosses that fence into trailing prose is not promised, because the unwrapped fence's visible text is not the title's words, and making it so is a renderer change this lane was forbidden to make. Pin: neither, never one side.\n\n**pr** — source offsets threaded through the title render; the old neither-piece pin flipped positive; fence crossing pinned neither-not-half as the honest remainder","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:55:59-04:00","custom":{"from":"#240, narrowed by #254","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/725ec411","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/316"}}
{"id":"palette-count-cap","parent":"search","ord":"aK","title":"The palette and header search cap at 8 hits #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-20T21:25:25-04:00","desc":"Filed at #248's merge (the count-line honesty PR).\n\n- The filtered page's count line now tells all three truths, but the ⌘K palette and the header search box still cap at 8 drawn hits with no denominator — `SearchAnswer.total` is already on the wire and uncounted.\n- Different surface, denominator and hider than the page's count line; also noted in docs/brainstorming/filter-in-place.md.\n\n**pr** — 2026-08-20 — total off the same answer as hits; count.ts sentence + Count.tsx in both doors; picker panels excluded by ruling written into docs/search.md","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:09-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:55:59-04:00","custom":{"from":"#248","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/481cbe6e","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/306"}}
{"id":"preview-postload-growth","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aG","title":"A previewed page that grows after loading never gets a taller frame #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T09:52:50-04:00","desc":"#206's deferral 5 — found by three refactor checks and confirmed by a verifier; predates #206, but running JavaScript is exactly what makes drawing late content common, so #206 makes it matter.\n- **Symptom:** a chart drawn from a fetch, a details element the reader opens, a late web font — the frame keeps its pre-growth height.\n- **Converged fix:** instead of rationing height reports per width, accept reports but REJECT THE ECHO — a report within a pixel or two of the frame's own current height is a vh-page feeding its container back; everything else is honest growth.\n- A behavior change wanting its own scenario.\n\n**pr** — the node's within-a-pixel rule disproven by measurement; shipped: echo = unchanged gap over the frame + TURNS + one height per painted frame","created":"2026-08-16T13:46:29-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"206","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/4581aefb","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/313"}}
{"id":"doc-page-props","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aH","title":"Where should a document page show its own properties? #deferral #needs-brainstorm #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T15:48:27-04:00","desc":"- RULED and shipped by #322 (523e2d3d): properties draw under the path heading, above Contents — custom keys only, honest absence, hidden while editing (pinned in documents.feature), no Add-property affordance (writing the block is editing the file).\n- list_documents unlocked in the same change: reports props, omitted when empty, unreadable carries none — MCP and Web are one answer.\n- The #302-era sentence 'list_documents deliberately reports no props until this is ruled' retired with the ruling (opencode's finding 3).","created":"2026-08-20T19:53:42-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"#302"}}
{"id":"perf-patch-residue","parent":"infra-model","ord":"aH","title":"The patcher still allocates every record and clones ten indexes per patch #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T16:42:41-04:00","desc":"- **Shipped WHOLE by PR #323** (commit 0c8a885c). The dispatch overrode the earlier ruling that only the medium-sized half was in scope, and the large half landed too: the flat array of all records is now built lazily (the one caller that checks shapes walks file by file instead), the overlay learned how to delete and append, and every index is classified by its reader in an exhaustive table the typechecker enforces (7 layers, 4 maps — `byFile` was timed and deliberately left as a clone, at 0.174ms against 0.241ms).\n- The documentation's old claim that \"a layer cannot delete\" was corrected in overlay.ts, the format README, architecture.md and model-indices.md.\n- A patch went from 0.78ms to 0.45ms against the branch point (about 115 times faster than rebuilding from scratch); carrying layers forward is pinned by a chained property test (100 corpora, 12 folded edits each, compared against a full derive, 12 revisions deep).\n\n**Verified against master commit 44bc6873, under the human's scope ruling** — medium half only that night: the flat `[...ordered.values()].flat()` at patch.ts line 293 (load-bearing, via `Derived.nodes`) and the `new Map(byFile)` churn at patch.ts line 267. The clone list is now TEN (`byDay` joined at PR #278; benchmark at patch.bench.ts lines 435-436), but the browser side of the claim is dead (the fold was deleted by the flip), and removing the ten clones needs a delete-capable overlay that the docs argue against — so that large half stays deferred, with these facts recorded.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:09-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferral (the patcher's flat-list allocation), quantified by the O(n) sweep audit","verified":"2026-08-20"}}
{"id":"perf-faces-broken-walk","parent":"bug-server","ord":"aF","title":"faces/broken walks every key per frame #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T09:06:54-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 at PR #265's merge (it had ridden along on PR #263 as its third deferral; #265 numbered it without touching it).\n- The code computing per-file faces and broken-ness walks every key on every frame; measured at +0.1 to +0.3ms of a roughly 4.5ms frame (the spread is stated where the numbers live, packages/web/README.md).\n- The `/simplify` pass in #265 found the cheaper form for whoever picks this up — the note is in that PR's refactor commits.\n- Deliberately untouched by #265 — it was not one of that PR's four items.\n\n**PR:** one walk producing faces, broken-ness and paths together. The related fold over `heads` was deferred for a strong, reviewed reason and filed separately as directory-heads-fold.\n\n**Verified against master commit 44bc6873:** it still APPLIES exactly as written — directory.ts lines 107-140 names this node in its own comment; the faces computation has no equality check, and broken-ness pays the same walk; `facesOf` still flatMaps per file. **Caveat:** the benchmark the quoted numbers came from (outlines.bench.ts) was deleted by PR #279, and packages/web/README.md no longer carries them, so the evidence must now be a run-count browser test probe rather than a benchmark. The cheaper form from #265 still applies exactly: one merged walk producing both.","created":"2026-08-19T19:39:07-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:08-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferral 3, requantified by #265","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/50baf9b1","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/311","verified":"2026-08-20"}}
{"id":"e2e-underload-full-census","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"aG","title":"e2e: run the full-suite flake census at scale #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T08:02:42-04:00","desc":"Run the full-suite flake census at scale — `underload.sh RUNS=20 BUSY=48` / `SUITES=5` — after the scratch-sharing change.\n\nFiled 2026-08-20 at #281's merge (opencode: verification work not yet run — a deferral, not a finding).\n- #281 ran underload.sh on the two converted files only (RUNS=3: 3 runs, 0 drops). The full-suite run at the census's own settings takes hours and the spawn saving was 16 of 502, so the lane did not pay for it.\n- Worth running once, unattended, to learn whether the port/lock failure class moved at all and to re-baseline the census after the ~150-scenario cut and the sharing change. Output is a number in the README's census paragraph, not a code change.\n\n**pr** — census re-baselined on kolu-ci-6 at 399cf308; numbers in packages/tests/README.md","created":"2026-08-20T11:06:24-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:09-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #281 deferral","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/c72e4be7","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/309","superseded":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the 2026-08-21 census (kolu-ci-6 @ 399cf308) is superseded — the classes it counted-not-fixed (scroll-restore 267px, CSP picture, 15s waits) were FIXED by #363, and the unit races by #347/#359/#360/#361/#364; the suite's waiting doctrine grew to five classes. Any re-baseline runs post-#363 on the currently ruled venue (kolu-ci-* usable again as of today)"}}
{"id":"preview-atx-regex","parent":"feat-docs","ord":"aI","title":"preview.ts still carries the quadratic heading-trim regex #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T16:08:27-04:00","desc":"- Shipped by #321 (0520ace5): plainLine scans from the end like slug.ts's headingText; the quadratic /\\s+#+$/ is gone (red-first pin: 1594ms→11ms on 50k spaces).\n- The scan deliberately narrows to space/tab (CommonMark; agrees with headingText) — named in a comment and pinned ('# Foo ##' keeps its hashes). Class sweep: zero live sites remain; CodeQL green.","created":"2026-08-20T22:20:33-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"#304"}}
{"id":"said-home-and-nudge","parent":"feat-kbd","ord":"aB","title":"SaidLine's home, and whether the editor's nudge speaks #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T12:26:16-04:00","desc":"Two leftovers from #310: (1) the editor's refusal carries data-kind and its nudge sibling has no role/aria-live — routing them through SaidLine would CHANGE what a screen reader is told (role=status aria-live=polite), a behavior ruling, plus a data-kind passthrough beside data-tone. (2) SaidLine still lives under edit/ with fourteen importers across eleven directories; moving it drags the Said type out of edit/undoing.ts — a where-does-the-two-mood-type-belong design question, not a file move.\n\n**pr** — SaidLine at the client top with the Said type; data-kind beside data-tone; the nudge speaks (role=status polite, red-first); a third hand-rolled hold-out folded; the only-SaidLine-reads-a-mood sweep","created":"2026-08-21T07:41:57-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:09-04:00","custom":{"from":"#310","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/6b077271","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/318"}}
{"id":"directory-heads-fold","parent":"bug-server","ord":"aE","title":"The directory rides heads' collection fold #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T12:00:18-04:00","desc":"PR #311 halved the constant cost — one walk per frame, with paths carried out of it — but a frame that names a single file still reads every file, re-sorts whenever membership moves, and creates a fresh paths array.\n\nThe `heads` data is served as batched deltas, so the delivery already knows which keys moved, and @kolu/surface exposes that as a collection fold — the same mechanism chat/order.ts used to retire the transcript's per-frame sort.\n\nThis was deferred at PR #311 for a strong, twice-reviewed reason:\n- A fold inherits \"invalidated until the next snapshot\" semantics, a state this directory has no answer for; the manifest cell's three-state argument would have to absorb it.\n- It needs an accumulator that maintains path order incrementally — chat/order.ts's `ordered()` works over a comparator rather than a number.\n- It also widens the HeadEntries interface, because a fold is registered rather than read.\n\n`walkOf`'s doc comment and the \"What is still whole-set\" section of packages/web/README.md both point here.\n\n**PR:** `SERVED_FILES` rides the collection fold; a frame costs only that frame; the absent state is absorbed by the manifest.","created":"2026-08-21T09:06:54-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:08-04:00","custom":{"from":"#311","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/99c3c26f","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/317"}}
{"id":"refusal-constructor-home","parent":"bug-server","ord":"aG","title":"The refusal constructors' home: pure reads import from the write planner #deferral #deferred","done":"2026-08-21T16:44:41-04:00","desc":"- Shipped by #326 (4d097252): refusals.ts holds the eight constructors (bodies byte-identical), plan.ts sheds them plus seven unused imports, query.ts/index.ts repointed, package surface unchanged, existing suites untouched-green.\n- Born as #320's deferral under the old review-burden reading; the human struck that criterion (instructions.md e5e06484) and this closed the same hour.","created":"2026-08-21T14:56:20-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:08-04:00","custom":{"from":"#320","overruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~16:4x — the 'godly' judgment is struck: diff size / review burden is NOT a deferral criterion (PRs mostly merge without human review); refactors spotted in a PR belong in that PR. Executed now as its own lane since #320 already merged."}}
{"id":"semantic-recall-parked","parent":"search","ord":"aG","title":"Semantic recall — built, reviewed, parked (draft PR #165) #someday","cancelled":"2026-09-01T14:53:30-04:00","desc":"RULED (the human, 2026-09-01, at the eighth sitting's ratification): **DROPPED.** The revival does not happen — neither as plugin-recall nor core-first; the sitting's contributed-matcher hook design stays on record in projects/olai/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-31.md should the question ever reopen. Draft PR #165 is the human's own and stays theirs to close.","changed":"2026-09-06T15:55:59-04:00","custom":{"refit-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: the resume list is stale — the cited design doc lives only on the semantic-recall branch (not master); the re-fit target is no longer #167/#168 but addresses (#256), the six-kind Bodied arm (#362 widened filter.ts), and the coming @olai/child (recall/embedder.ts is gone from master; the package must CONSUME @olai/child on return — see child-receptacle)"}}
{"id":"reminders-notifications","parent":"feat-dates","ord":"a6","title":"Reminders: nothing ever alerts you about due work #needs-brainstorm #someday","todo":true,"desc":"- Repeats and the agenda exist, but nothing notifies — no reminders, no due alerts, anywhere.\n- To decide in a brainstorm: the channel (browser notifications, the chat agent speaking up, OS-level), and the trigger (a date arriving, a repeat coming due, the agenda going non-empty).\n- Or rule that olai is deliberately pull-only — and write that down, since today the absence is stated nowhere.","created":"2026-08-20T17:40:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:07-04:00","custom":{"channel-answered":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: \"nothing notifies anywhere\" is no longer true — #358 shipped the whole alert CHANNEL as a reusable app-root seam (notify.ts over @kolu/surface-app/notify, click payload deliberately a shared union with \"one arm today\"; chime, PWA badge, prefs row, served SW). What this node still owns is only the TRIGGER (a date arriving, a repeat due, the agenda going non-empty) and the pull-only ruling","from":"repo survey 2026-08-20 (Opus explore agent), on the human's ask"}}
{"id":"graph-view","parent":"feat-nav","ord":"aH","title":"Graph view: the reference graph as a navigable map #someday","todo":true,"desc":"- `/graph/<id>` shows a node's neighbourhood; `/graph` the whole reference graph. Click to navigate; files drawn as groupings.\n- PR #247 built it but is parked as a draft: the human found it unsatisfying because .md documents aren't in the graph, and bolting that on would be messy.\n- Waits on the nodes/documents unification design (brainstorming/first-class-documents.md); rebuild on addresses once that lands.\n\n**pr** — parked as draft 2026-08-19 — the human ruled it unsatisfying: no .md/.olai parity, and bolting parity on would make a ball of mud; waits on the nodes/docs unification architecture (brainstorming doc)","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:49-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:00-04:00","custom":{"blocker-restated":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: \"rebuild on addresses once that lands\" — addresses LANDED at #256 (PR 1 of first-class-documents.md's path); the live blocker is PR 2 (the one Document collection — set.ts:74 still carries a separate documents array). Note also the graph's absent file set is now SIX kinds wide (#362 gave csv/pdf/pictures addresses and pages, no vertices)","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/247","unblocked-by":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md — rebuilt on addresses at step 4 of its path"}}
{"id":"search-document-bodies","parent":"search","ord":"aF","title":"Search inside HTML documents — needs a ruling first #needs-brainstorm #someday","todo":true,"desc":"- Search already covers markdown document bodies (shipped with #258).\n- What's left: `.html` files. Their text isn't searchable because the server deliberately doesn't keep HTML bodies in memory (they can be megabytes).\n- Needs a decision before any code: either declare HTML opaque to search and close this, or design an index that reads bodies at search time without loading them all.\n- Related: the parked semantic-recall work.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-06T15:55:59-04:00","custom":{"scope-widened":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the remainder is no longer just .html — #362 added csv (holds:text, kept:false — the identical not-in-memory argument) and picture/pdf (holds:bytes — a different question: extraction, not memory); all share filter.ts's Unkept Bodied arm, whose own docstring (\"a .md and a .html alike\") is now stale. The ruling this node wants splits in two: text-but-unkept (.html, .csv) vs bytes (.pdf, pictures). Cross-link: first-class-documents.md PR 2 claims to close this node"}}
{"id":"hindsight-comparison","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"aJ","title":"Olai vs Hindsight: which agent-memory features are worth adopting #needs-brainstorm #someday","todo":true,"desc":"- Comparison against hindsight.vectorize.io, keeping files as the single source of truth. Brainstorm: docs/brainstorming/hindsight.md.\n- Six recommendations: semantic search as a derived gitignored index; time/graph recall as query clauses; capture-as-proposal at conversation end; consolidation as a stale/duplicates reading; per-connection scoping for multiple agents; sync stays git.\n- Deliberately not copied: LLM-normalized notes, identity config, hosted memory.\n- Awaits the human's picks.","changed":"2026-09-06T15:56:07-04:00","custom":{"rec5-answered":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: recommendation 5 (per-connection agent scoping) is settled AGAINST by master — listings.ts:4 rules one live agent always; the scoping arrived as listing-is-a-question fan-out (#343) + the per-conversation roster (#357). Recommendation 3's capture shape predates #354 (POST /capture retired for `olai surface capture`). The live remainder is picks 1, 2, 4 re-read against those"}}
